{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyKXSbvuvdJT7TjyW1u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018wErcqx7ihmrNmQzy6q8iD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/engine/repo/dist/handoff/modules/grid.js","limit":56},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2175,"cache_read_input_tokens":133387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2175},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"188d6a1f-a99c-4349-b0c9-2215d88ccc74","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:41.048Z","request_id":"req_011CggyKXFC4oj1N5pF2xhqK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018wErcqx7ihmrNmQzy6q8iD":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/engine/repo/dist/handoff/modules/grid.js","limit":56}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018wErcqx7ihmrNmQzy6q8iD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*!\n2\tmy-3D2dge module GRID v0.85.2: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns\n3\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n4\tLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n5\t\n6\tFor roguelikes, tactics, puzzles, mazes, board games and strategy's fog (what Godot calls AStarGrid2D). A cell is\n7\t[cx, cy]; a grid knows its size, which cells can be walked and what entering one costs, and nothing else: the game\n8\tkeeps its units.\n9\t- new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: false | 'pointy' | 'flat', walkable(cx, cy), cost(cx, cy) (1), height(cx, cy) (0),\n10\t  opaque(cx, cy) (not walkable), diagonal: false }); E.Grid.from(map, { tops }) reads a TileMap (its walkable cells;\n11\t  tops: true stands on its walls' tops at their heights, for tactics). Hex grids are offset rows ('pointy') or columns\n12\t  ('flat'), odd ones shifted.\n13\t- grid.inside(c), grid.walk(c), grid.neighbours(c) (4, 8 with diagonal, or 6), grid.dist(a, b) (Manhattan; Chebyshev\n14\t  with diagonal; hex steps); grid.center(c, T) and grid.toCell(x, y, T): world points (hex: T across).\n15\t- grid.path(a, b, { blocked(cx, cy), climb, drop, ends }) -> [a, ..., b] or [] (A*, ties broken the same way every\n16\t  time; ends: true reaches b even when b can't be walked: an attack's target). grid.reach(a, budget, { blocked, climb,\n17\t  drop, pass }) -> { cells: [[cx, cy, cost]], has(c), cost(c), path(c) } (Dijkstra: a move range; climb and drop limit\n18\t  the height a step may rise and fall: a unit's jump, E.HEIGHTS.level (8) a level; pass(cx, cy): cells crossed but not\n19\t  stopped on, its allies).\n20\t- grid.line(a, b) (Bresenham, hex: steps), grid.sees(a, b) (no opaque cell between), grid.fov(c, radius) -> a Set of\n21\t  'cx,cy' (symmetric shadowcasting: what a sees sees it; hex: lines). grid.flood(c, same(cx, cy)) and grid.groups(key(cx,\n22\t  cy) -> a value or null) -> [[cells]] (equal neighbours: matches, chains, regions).\n23\t- Tactics: grid.shape(c, kind, n, dir) -> cells ('cross', 'diamond', 'square', 'ring', 'line', 'cone': areas of\n24\t  effect); grid.face(a, b) (the four-way facing from a toward b); grid.side(at, facing, from) -> 'front' | 'side' |\n25\t  'back' (a blow from behind); grid.threat(units, { blocked }) -> { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) } (what units\n26\t  { cx, cy, move, range: [min, max], climb, drop } can strike next turn: an AI's safe cells). Over a TileMap's tops:\n27\t  map.pick(sx, sy) the cell under the pointer, map.arcClear(from, to, apex) a bow's arc.\n28\t- E.Fog(grid): fog.update([{ cx, cy, r }]) (each viewer's field of view: visible now; seen stays), fog.visible(c),\n29\t  fog.seen(c), fog.draw(r, T, o) (unseen black, seen dimmed: over the walls too, before your HUD); E.tint(r, cells, color,\n30\t  alpha, T, height): tints on cells' tops (ranges, paths).\n31\t- E.GridMover({ cx, cy, speed }) moves a cell at a time: mover.update(dt, grid, [dx, dy], { blocked, push(cx, cy, dx, dy),\n32\t  keep: true (on in the same way until blocked: Pac-Man) }): a turn asked early is kept and taken at the first opening (Pac-Man), push moves what is in the way (Sokoban);\n33\t  x, y: its smooth position in cells; moving, dir, arrived (true the step it reaches a cell).\n34\t- E.Turns(actors, { mode, sides (phase: their order), fill (atb: a gauge a second at speed 100, 1) }) says who acts: 'speed' (energy: each actor's speed, 100 a turn; a bat of 200 acts twice:\n35\t  roguelikes), 'ct' (charge time, the order ahead: Final Fantasy Tactics), 'phase' (every one of a side, then the next\n36\t  side: Fire Emblem; actor.side), 'atb' (gauges filled on game time: Final Fantasy). turns.next() -> the actor to act\n37\t  (speed, ct, phase); turns.order(n): who acts next, n of them; turns.update(dt) and turns.ready() (atb: those full),\n38\t  turns.done(actor, cost) (after it acted: ct and atb); add(a), remove(a).\n39\t\n40\t```js grid\n41\tconst E = My3D2dge, g = new E.Grid(8, 6, { walkable: (x, y) => !(x === 3 && y < 4) });\n42\tconst p = g.path([0, 0], [7, 0]); if (p.length !== 16 || p[0].join() !== '0,0') throw new Error('path ' + p.length);\n43\tconst r = g.reach([0, 0], 3); if (!r.has([0, 3]) || r.has([3, 4]) || r.cost([2, 1]) !== 3) throw new Error('reach');\n44\tconst fov = g.fov([1, 1], 6); if (fov.has('6,1') || !fov.has('3,1')) throw new Error('fov');\n45\tconst t = new E.Turns([{ id: 'hero', speed: 100 }, { id: 'bat', speed: 200 }], { mode: 'speed' });\n46\tif ([1, 2, 3].map(() => t.next().id).join() !== 'bat,hero,bat') throw new Error('turns');\n47\tif (g.shape([5, 2], 'cross', 1).length !== 5 || g.side([5, 2], [1, 0], [4, 2]) !== 'back') throw new Error('tactics');\n48\t```\n49\tRules: cells are whole numbers; paths and reaches never cross a cell blocked(cx, cy) says is taken (other units); the\n50\tsame inputs give the same paths, fields and turns. Draw the fog after the world and before your HUD.\n51\t*/\n52\t(function (E) {\n53\t'use strict';\n54\tif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module GRID: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n55\t\n56\t/* ============================================================================="}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"02eada9b-704d-4c60-8e21-1d6a34a50ed3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:41.055Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/engine/repo/dist/handoff/modules/grid.js","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module GRID v0.85.2: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nFor roguelikes, tactics, puzzles, mazes, board games and strategy's fog (what Godot calls AStarGrid2D). A cell is\n[cx, cy]; a grid knows its size, which cells can be walked and what entering one costs, and nothing else: the game\nkeeps its units.\n- new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: false | 'pointy' | 'flat', walkable(cx, cy), cost(cx, cy) (1), height(cx, cy) (0),\n  opaque(cx, cy) (not walkable), diagonal: false }); E.Grid.from(map, { tops }) reads a TileMap (its walkable cells;\n  tops: true stands on its walls' tops at their heights, for tactics). Hex grids are offset rows ('pointy') or columns\n  ('flat'), odd ones shifted.\n- grid.inside(c), grid.walk(c), grid.neighbours(c) (4, 8 with diagonal, or 6), grid.dist(a, b) (Manhattan; Chebyshev\n  with diagonal; hex steps); grid.center(c, T) and grid.toCell(x, y, T): world points (hex: T across).\n- grid.path(a, b, { blocked(cx, cy), climb, drop, ends }) -> [a, ..., b] or [] (A*, ties broken the same way every\n  time; ends: true reaches b even when b can't be walked: an attack's target). grid.reach(a, budget, { blocked, climb,\n  drop, pass }) -> { cells: [[cx, cy, cost]], has(c), cost(c), path(c) } (Dijkstra: a move range; climb and drop limit\n  the height a step may rise and fall: a unit's jump, E.HEIGHTS.level (8) a level; pass(cx, cy): cells crossed but not\n  stopped on, its allies).\n- grid.line(a, b) (Bresenham, hex: steps), grid.sees(a, b) (no opaque cell between), grid.fov(c, radius) -> a Set of\n  'cx,cy' (symmetric shadowcasting: what a sees sees it; hex: lines). grid.flood(c, same(cx, cy)) and grid.groups(key(cx,\n  cy) -> a value or null) -> [[cells]] (equal neighbours: matches, chains, regions).\n- Tactics: grid.shape(c, kind, n, dir) -> cells ('cross', 'diamond', 'square', 'ring', 'line', 'cone': areas of\n  effect); grid.face(a, b) (the four-way facing from a toward b); grid.side(at, facing, from) -> 'front' | 'side' |\n  'back' (a blow from behind); grid.threat(units, { blocked }) -> { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) } (what units\n  { cx, cy, move, range: [min, max], climb, drop } can strike next turn: an AI's safe cells). Over a TileMap's tops:\n  map.pick(sx, sy) the cell under the pointer, map.arcClear(from, to, apex) a bow's arc.\n- E.Fog(grid): fog.update([{ cx, cy, r }]) (each viewer's field of view: visible now; seen stays), fog.visible(c),\n  fog.seen(c), fog.draw(r, T, o) (unseen black, seen dimmed: over the walls too, before your HUD); E.tint(r, cells, color,\n  alpha, T, height): tints on cells' tops (ranges, paths).\n- E.GridMover({ cx, cy, speed }) moves a cell at a time: mover.update(dt, grid, [dx, dy], { blocked, push(cx, cy, dx, dy),\n  keep: true (on in the same way until blocked: Pac-Man) }): a turn asked early is kept and taken at the first opening (Pac-Man), push moves what is in the way (Sokoban);\n  x, y: its smooth position in cells; moving, dir, arrived (true the step it reaches a cell).\n- E.Turns(actors, { mode, sides (phase: their order), fill (atb: a gauge a second at speed 100, 1) }) says who acts: 'speed' (energy: each actor's speed, 100 a turn; a bat of 200 acts twice:\n  roguelikes), 'ct' (charge time, the order ahead: Final Fantasy Tactics), 'phase' (every one of a side, then the next\n  side: Fire Emblem; actor.side), 'atb' (gauges filled on game time: Final Fantasy). turns.next() -> the actor to act\n  (speed, ct, phase); turns.order(n): who acts next, n of them; turns.update(dt) and turns.ready() (atb: those full),\n  turns.done(actor, cost) (after it acted: ct and atb); add(a), remove(a).\n\n```js grid\nconst E = My3D2dge, g = new E.Grid(8, 6, { walkable: (x, y) => !(x === 3 && y < 4) });\nconst p = g.path([0, 0], [7, 0]); if (p.length !== 16 || p[0].join() !== '0,0') throw new Error('path ' + p.length);\nconst r = g.reach([0, 0], 3); if (!r.has([0, 3]) || r.has([3, 4]) || r.cost([2, 1]) !== 3) throw new Error('reach');\nconst fov = g.fov([1, 1], 6); if (fov.has('6,1') || !fov.has('3,1')) throw new Error('fov');\nconst t = new E.Turns([{ id: 'hero', speed: 100 }, { id: 'bat', speed: 200 }], { mode: 'speed' });\nif ([1, 2, 3].map(() => t.next().id).join() !== 'bat,hero,bat') throw new Error('turns');\nif (g.shape([5, 2], 'cross', 1).length !== 5 || g.side([5, 2], [1, 0], [4, 2]) !== 'back') throw new Error('tactics');\n```\nRules: cells are whole numbers; paths and reaches never cross a cell blocked(cx, cy) says is taken (other units); the\nsame inputs give the same paths, fields and turns. Draw the fog after the world and before your HUD.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module GRID: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":409}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018wErcqx7ihmrNmQzy6q8iD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
