{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012mDTdJD94tF4kmCbdwgdBF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t160: * SLICE 15  TACTICS  (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Shining Force, Fire Emblem). @modules grid story\n2\t161: * THE TAKING OF THORNWATCH: four heroes storm a hill fort held by the Ash Legion's five (Grimwald, the knight who leads\n3\t162: * them, at the gate; an archer on the wall; a mage on the tower; a priest in the yard; a thief out on the hills). An\n4\t163: * isometric map of heights (E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, a level): a unit walks MOVE cells, climbs and drops what its JUMP allows,\n5\t164: * and the river's shallows cost two. Blows land harder from the side (x1.25) and from behind (x1.5) and from higher\n6\t165: * ground (+8% a level). Turns come by speed (charge time: the order ahead is on the left) or, picked before the battle,\n7\t166: * by phases (every hero in the order you like, then every foe: Fire Emblem). A turn: MOVE and ACT once each, either\n8\t167: * first (ATTACK or the unit's skill), then WAIT and face a way. Bows arc over what stands between (map.arcClear) and\n9\t168: * reach further from up high; FIRE burns a diamond (friend and foe alike), VOLLEY rains on a cross, CURE heals one,\n10\t169: * BASH knocks a foe back a cell, CLEAVE cuts the three cells ahead. The Legion scores every place it can stand and every\n11\t170: * blow it can strike from there (the damage, a kill, a heal, the danger of the place: grid.threat). Win: the Legion falls.\n12\t171: * Lose: every hero falls.\n13\t172: * Keys: arrows / WASD move the cursor (the camera follows), Enter / Z confirm, Esc / X back (before acting, back undoes a\n14\t173: * move), Q and E turn the view a quarter, the wheel or - and = zoom. The mouse: the cursor follows the pointer\n15\t174: * (map.pick, the cell under it in every view and turn); a click confirms. TOUCH: a tap selects a unit, a tap on a blue\n16\t175: * cell moves there, a tap on a foe in range strikes; the command list's rows are a thumb's height; a finger dragging\n17\t176: * pans the camera, two pinch it; TURN turns the view.\n18\t177: * HOW IT WORKS: the map is a TileMap whose cells all stand on a base (the earth shows at its edges) at their heights; the\n19\t178: * grid is E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true }) with the shallows' cost; E.Turns ('ct') orders the turns, grid.reach the\n20\t179: * moves (allies passed through), grid.shape the areas, grid.side where a blow lands, grid.threat the AI's danger; E.Story\n21\t180: * runs the scene before the battle and its choice of the order. bot() lets the heroes' own AI play the battle\n22\t181: * (tools/kits-test.mjs). Deep links: #tactics/battle (no scene, charge time), #tactics/phases.\n23\t182: * ===================================================================================== */\n24\t183:const TACTICS = (() => {\n25\t690:scenes.tactics = TACTICS;\n26\t692:/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n27\t694:for (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\n28\t695:titleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n29\t698:const [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"2d940d4a-daa3-4118-947f-259b6d29c38a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:55.034Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/out7.txt","content":"160: * SLICE 15  TACTICS  (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Shining Force, Fire Emblem). @modules grid story\n161: * THE TAKING OF THORNWATCH: four heroes storm a hill fort held by the Ash Legion's five (Grimwald, the knight who leads\n162: * them, at the gate; an archer on the wall; a mage on the tower; a priest in the yard; a thief out on the hills). An\n163: * isometric map of heights (E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, a level): a unit walks MOVE cells, climbs and drops what its JUMP allows,\n164: * and the river's shallows cost two. Blows land harder from the side (x1.25) and from behind (x1.5) and from higher\n165: * ground (+8% a level). Turns come by speed (charge time: the order ahead is on the left) or, picked before the battle,\n166: * by phases (every hero in the order you like, then every foe: Fire Emblem). A turn: MOVE and ACT once each, either\n167: * first (ATTACK or the unit's skill), then WAIT and face a way. Bows arc over what stands between (map.arcClear) and\n168: * reach further from up high; FIRE burns a diamond (friend and foe alike), VOLLEY rains on a cross, CURE heals one,\n169: * BASH knocks a foe back a cell, CLEAVE cuts the three cells ahead. The Legion scores every place it can stand and every\n170: * blow it can strike from there (the damage, a kill, a heal, the danger of the place: grid.threat). Win: the Legion falls.\n171: * Lose: every hero falls.\n172: * Keys: arrows / WASD move the cursor (the camera follows), Enter / Z confirm, Esc / X back (before acting, back undoes a\n173: * move), Q and E turn the view a quarter, the wheel or - and = zoom. The mouse: the cursor follows the pointer\n174: * (map.pick, the cell under it in every view and turn); a click confirms. TOUCH: a tap selects a unit, a tap on a blue\n175: * cell moves there, a tap on a foe in range strikes; the command list's rows are a thumb's height; a finger dragging\n176: * pans the camera, two pinch it; TURN turns the view.\n177: * HOW IT WORKS: the map is a TileMap whose cells all stand on a base (the earth shows at its edges) at their heights; the\n178: * grid is E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true }) with the shallows' cost; E.Turns ('ct') orders the turns, grid.reach the\n179: * moves (allies passed through), grid.shape the areas, grid.side where a blow lands, grid.threat the AI's danger; E.Story\n180: * runs the scene before the battle and its choice of the order. bot() lets the heroes' own AI play the battle\n181: * (tools/kits-test.mjs). Deep links: #tactics/battle (no scene, charge time), #tactics/phases.\n182: * ===================================================================================== */\n183:const TACTICS = (() => {\n690:scenes.tactics = TACTICS;\n692:/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n694:for (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\n695:titleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n698:const [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012mDTdJD94tF4kmCbdwgdBF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
