{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyNA2L3DjofLUJztjo5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ud78gJvMVBcUc72zhiy76L","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/out8.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":535,"cache_read_input_tokens":170114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":535},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"baacaf7d-22fb-422d-9f7d-7c2346268637","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:15.834Z","request_id":"req_011CggyN9mSvqUypTb3bW4zh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ud78gJvMVBcUc72zhiy76L":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/out8.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ud78gJvMVBcUc72zhiy76L","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=========== story\n2\t/*!\n3\tmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.85.2: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\n4\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n5\tLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n6\t\n7\tA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\n8\tE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n9\t- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n10\t  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n11\t  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n12\t  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n13\t- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n14\t  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n15\t    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n16\t  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n17\t  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n18\t    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n19\t    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n20\t  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n21\t    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n22\t- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n23\t  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n24\t- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n25\t  path), test(condition).\n26\t- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n27\t- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n28\t- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n29\t  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n30\t- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n31\t\n32\t```js story\n33\tconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\n34\tconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n35\t  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n36\t    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n37\t    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n38\t  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n39\t  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\n40\tgame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\n41\tconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\n42\tstory.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\n43\tif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\n44\tstory.run('elder'); press(2);\n45\tif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\n46\t```\n47\tRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\n48\tload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\n49\t*/\n50\t=========== arcade\n51\t/*!\n52\tmy-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.85.2: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\n53\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n54\tLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n55\t\n56\tWhat every coin-op had around its game: for arcade games, shooters, puzzles, pinball and brawlers.\n57\t- const cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'maze', lives: 3, extra: [10000] (or every: 20000), credits: null (free play;\n58\t  a number: coins a game, cab.coin() adds one), hud: true }); cab.start(players, { demo }) begins a game (one or two\n59\t  taking turns; false without the credits); cab.p is the player up ({ n, score, lives, save }), cab.players all.\n60\t- cab.add(points, at): the score (at: a world point { x, y, z }: the points float up there), an extra life at each\n61\t  threshold. cab.die() takes a life: 'again', 'next' (the other player's turn: \"PLAYER 2, READY!\"; keep each one's\n62\t  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n63\t- Tables, saved per game and mode: cab.table(mode) (the top ten { name, score }), cab.qualifies(score, mode),\n64\t  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n65\t  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n66\t- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n67\t- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n68\t  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n69\t  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n70\t- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n71\t  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n72\t\n73\t```js arcade\n74\tconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\n75\tcab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\n76\tif (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\n77\tif (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\n78\tcab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n79\t```\n80\tRules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\n81\tplaying the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n82\t*/\n83\t=========== strategy\n84\t/*!\n85\tmy-3D2dge module STRATEGY v0.85.2: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays\n86\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n87\tLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: grid.\n88\t\n89\tFor real-time strategy (Dune II, Warcraft II, Command & Conquer, StarCraft), builders and simulations (SimCity, Theme\n90\tPark, RollerCoaster Tycoon). It keeps the rules; the game draws (units are plain objects at x, y on a TileMap).\n91\t- const rts = new E.Strategy(game, { map, kinds, sides: { blue: { res: { gold: 300 } }, red: { res: { gold: 300 } } },\n92\t  player: 'blue', fog: true, on: { attack(u, t), death(u), made(u), built(b), gathered(u, n), ordered(at, u) } }).\n93\t  kinds[id]: a unit { hp, speed, r (5), tall (24: its bar's height), atk, range, rate (seconds a blow), sight (cells),\n94\t  cost: { gold: 50 }, time (to make), gather (a load) }, a building { building: true, w, h, hp, makes: ['worker'],\n95\t  depot: true, atk, range, cost, time } or a resource { resource: 'gold', amount, w, h }.\n96\t- rts.spawn(kind, side, x, y, { built: false }) -> { id, kind, side, K, x, y, r, hp, max, orders, face, moving, working,\n97\t  carry, progress, queue, rally } (a building's or resource's x, y: its middle, snapped to cells it blocks);\n98\t  rts.of(side, kind), rts.units, rts.remove(u), rts.side(id).res.\n99\t- rts.order(units, kind, target, { queue }): 'move' ({ x, y }), 'attack' (a unit), 'amove' ({ x, y }: fighting what it\n100\t  meets), 'gather' (a resource: trips to the nearest depot), 'build' ({ kind, cx, cy }: paid now), 'patrol' ({ x, y }),\n101\t  'stop'; queue: after the orders it has (Shift). A group moves in formation, slots round the point facing the way, on\n102\t  one flow field to it, kept apart; idle units fight what comes into sight. rts.smart(units, x, y, target): attack a foe,\n103\t  gather a resource, else move (a right click).\n104\t- rts.train(building, kind) (paid now, made after its time, sent to building.rally), rts.cancel(building),\n105\t  rts.afford(side, cost); rts.canPlace(kind, cx, cy) (free, walkable, seen); rts.ghost(r, kind, cx, cy) draws it.\n106\t- Selection, rts.input({ order: 'order' }) each step: a click or tap picks the player's unit under it (r.pick: draw them\n107\t  with { pick: u }) or none; input.box() selects the units inside; Shift adds; a double tap selects that kind on screen;\n108\t  Ctrl+1..9 keeps a group, 1..9 calls it; the order action (Mouse2) or a tap with a selection on ground, a foe or a\n109\t  resource gives rts.smart. rts.selected; rts.draw(r) after the world: rings, health bars, the box.\n110\t- rts.fog (E.Fog: the player's sight; walls block it), rts.visible(u); rts.minimap() is E.Shell's hud({ minimap }) (the\n111\t  fog, the camera's view, dots; a click moves the camera there).\n112\t- rts.ai(side, { build: [['worker', 5], ['barracks'], ['soldier', 6]], waves: { first: 90, every: 75, min: 4 }, script })\n113\t  works on the first step short of its count as it can pay (losses made again; buildings near its depot), keeps its\n114\t  workers mining nearest home and sends attack-moves at the nearest foe building; script(rts, side): a generator\n115\t  game.script runs. rts.update(dt) each step; rts.state() for a proof. A right click with a building that makes units\n116\t  selected sets its rally point.\n117\tTouch: a tap selects or orders, a drag on open ground pans (game.cam.free), a long press and a drag draws a box, a pinch\n118\tzooms. Time controls: game.timeScale 0, 1, 2, 4 (above 1, more steps of 1/120 s a frame, not longer ones).\n119\tSimulation:\n120\t- const clock = new E.Clock({ day: 240 (seconds), hour: 8 }); clock.update(dt); day, hour, minute, night, label()\n121\t  ('DAY 2  14:30'), light() -> { ambient: .1..1, color } (dark at night, warm at dawn and dusk).\n122\t- E.needs(agent, rates, dt) raises agent.needs ({ hunger: .2 }, 0..1) by rates a second; E.choose(agent, options) -> the\n123\t  option ({ gives: { hunger: -.6 }, x, y, cost }) that best meets its needs for the walk, or null.\n124\t- E.overlay(r, map, value(cx, cy) -> 0..1 or null, colors) tints cells by a value; E.tooltip(r, x, y, lines) a box.\n125\t\n126\t```js strategy\n127\tconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, view: 'topdown' }), map = new E.TileMap({ w: 20, h: 14 });\n128\tconst kinds = { hall: { building: true, w: 2, h: 2, hp: 300, depot: true, makes: ['worker'] }, mine: { resource: 'gold', amount: 500 },\n129\t  worker: { hp: 20, speed: 40, atk: 2, range: 10, rate: 1, sight: 5, cost: { gold: 50 }, time: 2, gather: 10 } };\n130\tconst rts = new E.Strategy(game, { map, kinds, sides: { blue: { res: { gold: 100 } } }, player: 'blue' });\n131\tconst hall = rts.spawn('hall', 'blue', 48, 48), mine = rts.spawn('mine', null, 216, 56), w = rts.spawn('worker', 'blue', 80, 60);\n132\tgame.start({ update(dt) { rts.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n133\trts.order([w], 'gather', mine); rts.train(hall, 'worker'); game.advance(20);\n134\tif (rts.side('blue').res.gold <= 50 || rts.of('blue', 'worker').length !== 2) throw new Error('gather, train');\n135\t```\n136\tRules: units are the module's; read them, draw them, give them orders; a building blocks its cells (map.block), so\n137\tflow fields go round it. The same orders give the same game.\n138\t*/\n139\t=========== songs\n140\t/*!\n141\tmy-3D2dge module SONGS v0.85.2: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood\n142\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n143\tLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n144\t\n145\tOriginal chiptunes in the step sequencer's format (game.audio.music's: { bpm, steps, tracks }), each with a title and\n146\tits moods, ready to play or to copy and change.\n147\t- E.Songbook.songs: every song by id; E.Songbook.get(id) -> the song; E.Songbook.find(mood) -> the ids of the songs of\n148\t  that mood (in the order they are listed); E.Songbook.moods: every mood there is.\n149\t- Moods: title, field, town, shop, calm, dungeon, battle, boss, race, puzzle, space, horror, stealth, chase, dance,\n150\t  and the jingles (loop: false): stage clear, game over, one-up, level up, fanfare.\n151\t- A song's tracks may have a name and on: false (a layer, silent until game.audio.layer(name, 1) brings it in, on the\n152\t  full engine): 'shadows' sneaks on three tracks and brings in 'chase' and 'alarm' when the guards see you.\n153\t- A song's len (steps) can run longer than its tracks (they loop on their own lengths within it): the dance songs.\n154\t\n155\t```js songs\n156\tconst E = My3D2dge, battle = E.Songbook.find('battle');\n157\tif (!battle.length || !E.Songbook.get(battle[0]).tracks.length) throw new Error('a battle song');\n158\tif (E.Songbook.get('clear').loop !== false || !E.Songbook.moods.includes('stealth')) throw new Error('jingles and moods');\n159\tfor (const id in E.Songbook.songs) for (const t of E.Songbook.songs[id].tracks) if (!t.notes.trim()) throw new Error(id);\n160\t```\n161\tRules: play one with game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get(id)) (a jingle: audio.sting, over the music, in the full engine); copy a song into\n162\tyour game to change it; a kit carries this module only when it plays its songs.\n163\t*/\n164\t=========== rpg\n165\t/*!\n166\tmy-3D2dge module RPG v0.85.2: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters\n167\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n168\tLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n169\t\n170\tThe systems under a JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, Chrono Trigger), and the inventory grid of a Resident Evil.\n171\t- const rpg = new E.RPG({ items, monsters, status, curve }). items: { id: { name, kind: 'use' | 'weapon' | 'armor' |\n172\t  'helm' | 'accessory' | 'key', price, stack (99), heal, mp, cure: ['poison'], revive (a share of HP), stats: { atk: 4 }\n173\t  (worn: slot = its kind), size: [w, h] (grid cells), icon (a sprite; else one for its kind), info } }. monsters: { id:\n174\t  { name, hp, atk, def, mag, spd, exp, gold, drops: [[chance, item]] } }. status: over the defaults (poison: a\n175\t  sixteenth of HP each tick; regen heals that; sleep and stop skip turns; silence bars skills; haste and slow change\n176\t  spd), each { turns (0: till cured), hurt, heal, skip, mute, spd }. curve(lv): the experience a level needs in all.\n177\t- const hero = rpg.member({ name, level, stats: { hp, mp, atk, def, mag, spd }, growth: { hp: 10, atk: 2 } (a level),\n178\t  equip: { weapon: 'sword' }, data }): hero.stat(k) (base, growth, gear, status), hero.max('hp'), hero.hp, mp, level,\n179\t  exp, next (to the next level), dead, data (the game's own); gain(exp) → the levels reached [{ level, up: { hp: 11 } }];\n180\t  equip(id, inv) (the old piece back into inv), unequip(slot, inv), compare(id) → { atk: 3, def: -1 } (equipping it); afflict(k, turns), cure(k) (k left out: all), has(k), acts() (no skip), tick() (a turn: hurt, heal,\n181\t  effects run out; → [[k, hp change or 'ends']]).\n182\t- const party = rpg.party([hero], { gold, inv }): members, alive, gold, inv (rpg.inventory() by default); use(id, m)\n183\t  (heal, mp, cure, revive; → true when it did something, and the item is gone); rest() (an inn); reward(troop) (monster\n184\t  ids, or { exp, gold, items }) → { exp, gold, items, levels: [[member, levels]] } (exp shared by the living).\n185\t- const inv = rpg.inventory({ slots: 32 } | { grid: [8, 5] }): add(id, n) (false, and nothing added, when it won't\n186\t  fit), remove(id, n), count(id), has(id, n), list() → [{ id, n, item, x, y }]; a grid's: fits(id, x, y), place(id, x,\n187\t  y), at(x, y).\n188\t- const shop = rpg.shop(['potion', 'sword']): price(id), worth(id) (selling: half), buy(party, id, n), sell(party, id,\n189\t  n) (→ true when done; key items don't sell).\n190\t- rpg.damage(a, b, { power: 1, kind: 'phys' | 'mag', crit: .08, guard }) → { hp, crit }: attack less half the defense\n191\t  (members' stats, or a monster's fields), a tenth either way; a critical hit ignores armor.\n192\t- const enc = rpg.encounters({ field: { every: [12, 28] (cells walked), troops: [[3, ['slime', 'slime']], [1, ['bat']]] } }):\n193\t  enc.walk(zone, units) each step → a troop when the count runs out (it starts again), else null.\n194\t- party.state() → JSON for a save; rpg.restore(state) → that party.\n195\t- Windows (in r.overlay): rpg.list(g, x, y, w, rows, { cursor, title, top, show, rowH, bg }) (rows: [{ label, note,\n196\t  icon, off }]; → { x, y, w, h, row(px, py): the row under a tap, at(i) }), rpg.card(g, x, y, member, { portrait } (full engine)),\n197\t  rpg.icon(id).\n198\t\n199\t```js rpg\n200\tconst E = My3D2dge, rpg = new E.RPG({ items: { potion: { name: 'Potion', kind: 'use', heal: 30, price: 10 }, sword: { name: 'Sword', kind: 'weapon', stats: { atk: 5 }, price: 60 } },\n201\t  monsters: { slime: { name: 'Slime', hp: 10, atk: 4, def: 1, exp: 9, gold: 6 } } });\n202\tconst hero = rpg.member({ name: 'Rowan', stats: { hp: 40, mp: 4, atk: 10, def: 4 }, growth: { hp: 8, atk: 2 } });\n203\tconst party = rpg.party([hero], { gold: 100 }), shop = rpg.shop(['potion', 'sword']);\n204\tif (!shop.buy(party, 'sword') || hero.compare('sword').atk !== 5 || !hero.equip('sword', party.inv) || hero.stat('atk') !== 15) throw new Error('a sword bought and worn');\n205\tconst won = party.reward(['slime', 'slime', 'slime', 'slime']);\n206\tif (won.exp !== 36 || party.gold !== 64 || hero.level < 2 || hero.max('hp') !== 40 + 8 * (hero.level - 1)) throw new Error('the reward, a level');\n207\thero.hp = 5; shop.buy(party, 'potion'); if (!party.use('potion', hero) || hero.hp !== 35 || party.inv.has('potion')) throw new Error('a potion drunk');\n208\tif (rpg.restore(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(party.state()))).members[0].stat('atk') !== hero.stat('atk')) throw new Error('saved and back');\n209\t```\n210\tRules: ids in the save, never objects; a battle reads members' stat() and writes their hp and mp back; draw windows\n211\tin r.overlay; randomness is Math.random's (a proof seeds it).\n212\t*/\n213\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"a5948098-826d-4d2d-b283-856fe48234c8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:15.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/out8.txt","content":"=========== story\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.85.2: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\nE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n  path), test(condition).\n- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n\n```js story\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\nif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);\nif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\n```\nRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\nload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\n*/\n=========== arcade\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.85.2: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nWhat every coin-op had around its game: for arcade games, shooters, puzzles, pinball and brawlers.\n- const cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'maze', lives: 3, extra: [10000] (or every: 20000), credits: null (free play;\n  a number: coins a game, cab.coin() adds one), hud: true }); cab.start(players, { demo }) begins a game (one or two\n  taking turns; false without the credits); cab.p is the player up ({ n, score, lives, save }), cab.players all.\n- cab.add(points, at): the score (at: a world point { x, y, z }: the points float up there), an extra life at each\n  threshold. cab.die() takes a life: 'again', 'next' (the other player's turn: \"PLAYER 2, READY!\"; keep each one's\n  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n- Tables, saved per game and mode: cab.table(mode) (the top ten { name, score }), cab.qualifies(score, mode),\n  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n\n```js arcade\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\ncab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\nif (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\nif (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\ncab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n```\nRules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\nplaying the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n*/\n=========== strategy\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STRATEGY v0.85.2: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: grid.\n\nFor real-time strategy (Dune II, Warcraft II, Command & Conquer, StarCraft), builders and simulations (SimCity, Theme\nPark, RollerCoaster Tycoon). It keeps the rules; the game draws (units are plain objects at x, y on a TileMap).\n- const rts = new E.Strategy(game, { map, kinds, sides: { blue: { res: { gold: 300 } }, red: { res: { gold: 300 } } },\n  player: 'blue', fog: true, on: { attack(u, t), death(u), made(u), built(b), gathered(u, n), ordered(at, u) } }).\n  kinds[id]: a unit { hp, speed, r (5), tall (24: its bar's height), atk, range, rate (seconds a blow), sight (cells),\n  cost: { gold: 50 }, time (to make), gather (a load) }, a building { building: true, w, h, hp, makes: ['worker'],\n  depot: true, atk, range, cost, time } or a resource { resource: 'gold', amount, w, h }.\n- rts.spawn(kind, side, x, y, { built: false }) -> { id, kind, side, K, x, y, r, hp, max, orders, face, moving, working,\n  carry, progress, queue, rally } (a building's or resource's x, y: its middle, snapped to cells it blocks);\n  rts.of(side, kind), rts.units, rts.remove(u), rts.side(id).res.\n- rts.order(units, kind, target, { queue }): 'move' ({ x, y }), 'attack' (a unit), 'amove' ({ x, y }: fighting what it\n  meets), 'gather' (a resource: trips to the nearest depot), 'build' ({ kind, cx, cy }: paid now), 'patrol' ({ x, y }),\n  'stop'; queue: after the orders it has (Shift). A group moves in formation, slots round the point facing the way, on\n  one flow field to it, kept apart; idle units fight what comes into sight. rts.smart(units, x, y, target): attack a foe,\n  gather a resource, else move (a right click).\n- rts.train(building, kind) (paid now, made after its time, sent to building.rally), rts.cancel(building),\n  rts.afford(side, cost); rts.canPlace(kind, cx, cy) (free, walkable, seen); rts.ghost(r, kind, cx, cy) draws it.\n- Selection, rts.input({ order: 'order' }) each step: a click or tap picks the player's unit under it (r.pick: draw them\n  with { pick: u }) or none; input.box() selects the units inside; Shift adds; a double tap selects that kind on screen;\n  Ctrl+1..9 keeps a group, 1..9 calls it; the order action (Mouse2) or a tap with a selection on ground, a foe or a\n  resource gives rts.smart. rts.selected; rts.draw(r) after the world: rings, health bars, the box.\n- rts.fog (E.Fog: the player's sight; walls block it), rts.visible(u); rts.minimap() is E.Shell's hud({ minimap }) (the\n  fog, the camera's view, dots; a click moves the camera there).\n- rts.ai(side, { build: [['worker', 5], ['barracks'], ['soldier', 6]], waves: { first: 90, every: 75, min: 4 }, script })\n  works on the first step short of its count as it can pay (losses made again; buildings near its depot), keeps its\n  workers mining nearest home and sends attack-moves at the nearest foe building; script(rts, side): a generator\n  game.script runs. rts.update(dt) each step; rts.state() for a proof. A right click with a building that makes units\n  selected sets its rally point.\nTouch: a tap selects or orders, a drag on open ground pans (game.cam.free), a long press and a drag draws a box, a pinch\nzooms. Time controls: game.timeScale 0, 1, 2, 4 (above 1, more steps of 1/120 s a frame, not longer ones).\nSimulation:\n- const clock = new E.Clock({ day: 240 (seconds), hour: 8 }); clock.update(dt); day, hour, minute, night, label()\n  ('DAY 2  14:30'), light() -> { ambient: .1..1, color } (dark at night, warm at dawn and dusk).\n- E.needs(agent, rates, dt) raises agent.needs ({ hunger: .2 }, 0..1) by rates a second; E.choose(agent, options) -> the\n  option ({ gives: { hunger: -.6 }, x, y, cost }) that best meets its needs for the walk, or null.\n- E.overlay(r, map, value(cx, cy) -> 0..1 or null, colors) tints cells by a value; E.tooltip(r, x, y, lines) a box.\n\n```js strategy\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, view: 'topdown' }), map = new E.TileMap({ w: 20, h: 14 });\nconst kinds = { hall: { building: true, w: 2, h: 2, hp: 300, depot: true, makes: ['worker'] }, mine: { resource: 'gold', amount: 500 },\n  worker: { hp: 20, speed: 40, atk: 2, range: 10, rate: 1, sight: 5, cost: { gold: 50 }, time: 2, gather: 10 } };\nconst rts = new E.Strategy(game, { map, kinds, sides: { blue: { res: { gold: 100 } } }, player: 'blue' });\nconst hall = rts.spawn('hall', 'blue', 48, 48), mine = rts.spawn('mine', null, 216, 56), w = rts.spawn('worker', 'blue', 80, 60);\ngame.start({ update(dt) { rts.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\nrts.order([w], 'gather', mine); rts.train(hall, 'worker'); game.advance(20);\nif (rts.side('blue').res.gold <= 50 || rts.of('blue', 'worker').length !== 2) throw new Error('gather, train');\n```\nRules: units are the module's; read them, draw them, give them orders; a building blocks its cells (map.block), so\nflow fields go round it. The same orders give the same game.\n*/\n=========== songs\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module SONGS v0.85.2: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOriginal chiptunes in the step sequencer's format (game.audio.music's: { bpm, steps, tracks }), each with a title and\nits moods, ready to play or to copy and change.\n- E.Songbook.songs: every song by id; E.Songbook.get(id) -> the song; E.Songbook.find(mood) -> the ids of the songs of\n  that mood (in the order they are listed); E.Songbook.moods: every mood there is.\n- Moods: title, field, town, shop, calm, dungeon, battle, boss, race, puzzle, space, horror, stealth, chase, dance,\n  and the jingles (loop: false): stage clear, game over, one-up, level up, fanfare.\n- A song's tracks may have a name and on: false (a layer, silent until game.audio.layer(name, 1) brings it in, on the\n  full engine): 'shadows' sneaks on three tracks and brings in 'chase' and 'alarm' when the guards see you.\n- A song's len (steps) can run longer than its tracks (they loop on their own lengths within it): the dance songs.\n\n```js songs\nconst E = My3D2dge, battle = E.Songbook.find('battle');\nif (!battle.length || !E.Songbook.get(battle[0]).tracks.length) throw new Error('a battle song');\nif (E.Songbook.get('clear').loop !== false || !E.Songbook.moods.includes('stealth')) throw new Error('jingles and moods');\nfor (const id in E.Songbook.songs) for (const t of E.Songbook.songs[id].tracks) if (!t.notes.trim()) throw new Error(id);\n```\nRules: play one with game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get(id)) (a jingle: audio.sting, over the music, in the full engine); copy a song into\nyour game to change it; a kit carries this module only when it plays its songs.\n*/\n=========== rpg\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RPG v0.85.2: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nThe systems under a JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, Chrono Trigger), and the inventory grid of a Resident Evil.\n- const rpg = new E.RPG({ items, monsters, status, curve }). items: { id: { name, kind: 'use' | 'weapon' | 'armor' |\n  'helm' | 'accessory' | 'key', price, stack (99), heal, mp, cure: ['poison'], revive (a share of HP), stats: { atk: 4 }\n  (worn: slot = its kind), size: [w, h] (grid cells), icon (a sprite; else one for its kind), info } }. monsters: { id:\n  { name, hp, atk, def, mag, spd, exp, gold, drops: [[chance, item]] } }. status: over the defaults (poison: a\n  sixteenth of HP each tick; regen heals that; sleep and stop skip turns; silence bars skills; haste and slow change\n  spd), each { turns (0: till cured), hurt, heal, skip, mute, spd }. curve(lv): the experience a level needs in all.\n- const hero = rpg.member({ name, level, stats: { hp, mp, atk, def, mag, spd }, growth: { hp: 10, atk: 2 } (a level),\n  equip: { weapon: 'sword' }, data }): hero.stat(k) (base, growth, gear, status), hero.max('hp'), hero.hp, mp, level,\n  exp, next (to the next level), dead, data (the game's own); gain(exp) → the levels reached [{ level, up: { hp: 11 } }];\n  equip(id, inv) (the old piece back into inv), unequip(slot, inv), compare(id) → { atk: 3, def: -1 } (equipping it); afflict(k, turns), cure(k) (k left out: all), has(k), acts() (no skip), tick() (a turn: hurt, heal,\n  effects run out; → [[k, hp change or 'ends']]).\n- const party = rpg.party([hero], { gold, inv }): members, alive, gold, inv (rpg.inventory() by default); use(id, m)\n  (heal, mp, cure, revive; → true when it did something, and the item is gone); rest() (an inn); reward(troop) (monster\n  ids, or { exp, gold, items }) → { exp, gold, items, levels: [[member, levels]] } (exp shared by the living).\n- const inv = rpg.inventory({ slots: 32 } | { grid: [8, 5] }): add(id, n) (false, and nothing added, when it won't\n  fit), remove(id, n), count(id), has(id, n), list() → [{ id, n, item, x, y }]; a grid's: fits(id, x, y), place(id, x,\n  y), at(x, y).\n- const shop = rpg.shop(['potion', 'sword']): price(id), worth(id) (selling: half), buy(party, id, n), sell(party, id,\n  n) (→ true when done; key items don't sell).\n- rpg.damage(a, b, { power: 1, kind: 'phys' | 'mag', crit: .08, guard }) → { hp, crit }: attack less half the defense\n  (members' stats, or a monster's fields), a tenth either way; a critical hit ignores armor.\n- const enc = rpg.encounters({ field: { every: [12, 28] (cells walked), troops: [[3, ['slime', 'slime']], [1, ['bat']]] } }):\n  enc.walk(zone, units) each step → a troop when the count runs out (it starts again), else null.\n- party.state() → JSON for a save; rpg.restore(state) → that party.\n- Windows (in r.overlay): rpg.list(g, x, y, w, rows, { cursor, title, top, show, rowH, bg }) (rows: [{ label, note,\n  icon, off }]; → { x, y, w, h, row(px, py): the row under a tap, at(i) }), rpg.card(g, x, y, member, { portrait } (full engine)),\n  rpg.icon(id).\n\n```js rpg\nconst E = My3D2dge, rpg = new E.RPG({ items: { potion: { name: 'Potion', kind: 'use', heal: 30, price: 10 }, sword: { name: 'Sword', kind: 'weapon', stats: { atk: 5 }, price: 60 } },\n  monsters: { slime: { name: 'Slime', hp: 10, atk: 4, def: 1, exp: 9, gold: 6 } } });\nconst hero = rpg.member({ name: 'Rowan', stats: { hp: 40, mp: 4, atk: 10, def: 4 }, growth: { hp: 8, atk: 2 } });\nconst party = rpg.party([hero], { gold: 100 }), shop = rpg.shop(['potion', 'sword']);\nif (!shop.buy(party, 'sword') || hero.compare('sword').atk !== 5 || !hero.equip('sword', party.inv) || hero.stat('atk') !== 15) throw new Error('a sword bought and worn');\nconst won = party.reward(['slime', 'slime', 'slime', 'slime']);\nif (won.exp !== 36 || party.gold !== 64 || hero.level < 2 || hero.max('hp') !== 40 + 8 * (hero.level - 1)) throw new Error('the reward, a level');\nhero.hp = 5; shop.buy(party, 'potion'); if (!party.use('potion', hero) || hero.hp !== 35 || party.inv.has('potion')) throw new Error('a potion drunk');\nif (rpg.restore(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(party.state()))).members[0].stat('atk') !== hero.stat('atk')) throw new Error('saved and back');\n```\nRules: ids in the save, never objects; a battle reads members' stat() and writes their hp and mp back; draw windows\nin r.overlay; randomness is Math.random's (a proof seeds it).\n*/\n","numLines":213,"startLine":1,"totalLines":213}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ud78gJvMVBcUc72zhiy76L","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
