{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L5XvwcnJUV2B4nRtWegrxs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Brigandine The Legend of Forsena gameplay organization phase attack phase rune knights monsters mana battle 12 turns\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Brigandine (video game)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine:_The_Legend_of_Runersia\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine: the legend of forsena\",\"url\":\"https://presentationbuilder.internationaltrucks.com/brigandine-legend-forsena-2\"},{\"title\":\"Game Brigandine The Legend Of Forsena Iso\",\"url\":\"https://southpolar.netlify.com/game-brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena-iso\"},{\"title\":\"Connect with us\",\"url\":\"https://well-played.com.au/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review\"},{\"title\":\"Connect with us\",\"url\":\"https://www.well-played.com.au/?p=424045\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review\",\"url\":\"https://turnbasedlovers.com/?p=28403\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine (video game)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"www.gamerbraves.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamerbraves.com/?p=58446\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review\",\"url\":\"https://turnbasedlovers.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-pc-version-review\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine the legend of runersia\",\"url\":\"https://www.nintendolife.com/reviews/switch-eshop/brigandine_the_legend_of_runersia\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Brigandine:_The_Legend_of_Runersia\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine (video game)\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine legend runersia review\",\"url\":\"https://techraptor.Net/gaming/reviews/brigandine-legend-runersia-review\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia Review\",\"url\":\"https://rpgamer.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review/\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine the legend of runersia review of monsters and muddles\",\"url\":\"https://www.gameskinny.com/reviews/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review-of-monsters-and-muddles/\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine : Abyss modernise le RPG tactique sur grille hexagonale\",\"url\":\"https://www.dlcompare.fr/actualites-gaming/brigandine-abyss-ressuscite-le-rpg-tactique-classique-83172\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Brigandine%3A_The_Legend_of_Runersia\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine the legend of runersia review\",\"url\":\"https://blastawaythegamereview.com/2021/01/18/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review/\"}]\n\nThe search covered the phase structure well, but it didn't turn up anything on mana or a 12-turn limit.\n\n- **Two phases per month or season:** Sources describe the game as split into an Organization phase and an Attack phase. Each month has an organize phase and an attack phase. Another source says that all six nations perform an Organization Phase and an Attack Phase in sequence. These combined actions are called a \"season\" and mark the passage of time.\n- **Organization phase:** Players move troops, set their composition, and decide which castles to attack. One source adds that whether to send idle Rune Knights on automated quests for rare items is also decided here. Summoning and reviving monsters is part of this phase too.\n- **Attack phase:** The turn-based battles make up the Attack Phase. Invasions happen when you can engage in as many invasions during the Attack phase as you feel you can handle.\n- **Naming:** Forsena is the 1998 PlayStation original (released in North America as The Legend of Forsena), and Runersia is the 2020 sequel with the same core gameplay in a new setting. It is a sequel to the 1998 PlayStation game Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena, and features the same core gameplay with a new setting.\n\nNot confirmed by these results: mana mechanics and a 12-turn battle limit. Searching for those specifically, perhaps with \"Brigandine battle turn limit\", would be the next step if you need them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"63369b2e-768d-413d-b4bc-bf9745fa7dd9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:28.700Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Brigandine The Legend of Forsena gameplay organization phase attack phase rune knights monsters mana battle 12 turns","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RoYafzQ3XP9PFhHnonXetE","content":[{"title":"Brigandine (video game)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine:_The_Legend_of_Runersia"},{"title":"brigandine: the legend of forsena","url":"https://presentationbuilder.internationaltrucks.com/brigandine-legend-forsena-2"},{"title":"Game Brigandine The Legend Of Forsena Iso","url":"https://southpolar.netlify.com/game-brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena-iso"},{"title":"Connect with us","url":"https://well-played.com.au/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review"},{"title":"Connect with us","url":"https://www.well-played.com.au/?p=424045"},{"title":"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review","url":"https://turnbasedlovers.com/?p=28403"},{"title":"Brigandine (video game)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)"},{"title":"www.gamerbraves.com","url":"https://www.gamerbraves.com/?p=58446"},{"title":"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review","url":"https://turnbasedlovers.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-pc-version-review"},{"title":"brigandine the legend of runersia","url":"https://www.nintendolife.com/reviews/switch-eshop/brigandine_the_legend_of_runersia"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Brigandine:_The_Legend_of_Runersia"},{"title":"Brigandine (video game)","url":"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)"},{"title":"brigandine legend runersia review","url":"https://techraptor.Net/gaming/reviews/brigandine-legend-runersia-review"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia Review","url":"https://rpgamer.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review/"},{"title":"brigandine the legend of runersia review of monsters and muddles","url":"https://www.gameskinny.com/reviews/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review-of-monsters-and-muddles/"},{"title":"Brigandine : Abyss modernise le RPG tactique sur grille hexagonale","url":"https://www.dlcompare.fr/actualites-gaming/brigandine-abyss-ressuscite-le-rpg-tactique-classique-83172"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Runersia","url":"https://en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Brigandine%3A_The_Legend_of_Runersia"},{"title":"brigandine the legend of runersia review","url":"https://blastawaythegamereview.com/2021/01/18/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-review/"}]},"The search covered the phase structure well, but it didn't turn up anything on mana or a 12-turn limit.\n\n- **Two phases per month or season:** Sources describe the game as split into an Organization phase and an Attack phase. Each month has an organize phase and an attack phase. Another source says that all six nations perform an Organization Phase and an Attack Phase in sequence. These combined actions are called a \"season\" and mark the passage of time.\n- **Organization phase:** Players move troops, set their composition, and decide which castles to attack. One source adds that whether to send idle Rune Knights on automated quests for rare items is also decided here. Summoning and reviving monsters is part of this phase too.\n- **Attack phase:** The turn-based battles make up the Attack Phase. Invasions happen when you can engage in as many invasions during the Attack phase as you feel you can handle.\n- **Naming:** Forsena is the 1998 PlayStation original (released in North America as The Legend of Forsena), and Runersia is the 2020 sequel with the same core gameplay in a new setting. It is a sequel to the 1998 PlayStation game Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena, and features the same core gameplay with a new setting.\n\nNot confirmed by these results: mana mechanics and a 12-turn battle limit. Searching for those specifically, perhaps with \"Brigandine battle turn limit\", would be the next step if you need them."],"durationSeconds":4.641221739000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L5XvwcnJUV2B4nRtWegrxs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XU9Z9bFQjxCAao9JK79aof","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Brigandine Legend of Forsena review story nations Almekia Norgard Esgares Zemeckis Lance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Brigandine (video game)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamerevolution.com/?p=34227\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamerevolution.com/review/34227-brigandine-review\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine Retroview\",\"url\":\"https://rpgamer.com/review/brigandine-review/\"},{\"title\":\"www.tvtropes.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/Brigandine\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\",\"url\":\"https://www.rpgfan.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine Retroview\",\"url\":\"https://rpgamer.com/?p=33505\"},{\"title\":\"Opens in a new tab\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgmagonline.com/?p=190042\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine: the legend of forsena\",\"url\":\"https://presentationbuilder.internationaltrucks.com/brigandine-legend-forsena-2\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-17308\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena - Game Poster\",\"url\":\"https://rpggamers.com/game/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena\"},{\"title\":\"🕹️ New release: Lunar Lander Beyond\",\"url\":\"https://www.mobygames.com/game/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine the Legend of Forsena\",\"url\":\"https://rawg.io/games/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review\",\"url\":\"https://turnbasedlovers.com/?p=28403\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\",\"url\":\"https://retro-replay.com/db/playstation/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review\",\"url\":\"https://turnbasedlovers.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-pc-version-review\"},{\"title\":\"brigandine the legend of forsena\",\"url\":\"https://nextquest.dev/games/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena\"},{\"title\":\"Brigandine (video game)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"User Score\",\"url\":\"https://legacy.prod.metacritic.com/game/switch/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia/user-reviews\"}]\n\nReviews of Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (1998) mostly agree that the story is weak, though the setting and nations get some credit.\n\n- **Setting and premise:** One source describes a coup in the kingdom of Almekia that thrusts the continent of Forsena into war, with the player choosing one of six nations to conquer the rest. Brigandine invites you into the war-torn continent of Forsena, where the kingdom of Almekia has fallen to a ruthless coup.\n- **Named figures:** The RPGFan review lists rulers including Cai of Caerleon, Lance, Prince of New Almekia, Lyonesse of Leonia, and Vaynard of Norgard. Cai, the Silent and Wise King of Caerleon; Lance the Prince of New Almekia; Lyonesee, Queen of Leonia; Vaynard, ruler of Norgard and Dryst, the Mad Duke of Iscalio. I didn't find a source describing Zemeckis's role in detail. One RPGamer retroview says dark forces were behind urging Zemeckis's actions, but the true architect of the continent-wide conflict is never fully addressed even by the story's conclusion.\n- **Critical reception:** Reviewers are harsh. RPGFan calls the story extremely thin. Game Revolution's verdict is blunt, listing the story as absolutely pitiful. The RPGamer retroview lists \"perfunctory story\" among its cons. A Metacritic user says the Forsena story has more twists, turning points, and less pacing issue than its sequel's.\n- **Story delivery:** Story arrives through brief dialogue. Game Revolution notes that Brigandine's \"story\" consists of short sequences of dialogue that occasionally pop up after every turn on the world map.\n\nOverall, the consensus is that the gameplay carries the game and the story is secondary. Retro Replay is the one outlier, praising the game excels in its branching story paths. Sources are mixed on whether the story is a flaw or an acceptable backdrop.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"c2e4627b-1ee4-462e-9727-342331dce4e9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:30.802Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Brigandine Legend of Forsena review story nations Almekia Norgard Esgares Zemeckis Lance","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FjzRxaJMnPyLrcTQri4rqQ","content":[{"title":"Brigandine (video game)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)"},{"title":"Brigandine Review","url":"https://www.gamerevolution.com/?p=34227"},{"title":"Brigandine Review","url":"https://www.gamerevolution.com/review/34227-brigandine-review"},{"title":"Brigandine Retroview","url":"https://rpgamer.com/review/brigandine-review/"},{"title":"www.tvtropes.org","url":"https://www.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/Brigandine"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena","url":"https://www.rpgfan.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena"},{"title":"Brigandine Retroview","url":"https://rpgamer.com/?p=33505"},{"title":"Opens in a new tab","url":"https://www.cgmagonline.com/?p=190042"},{"title":"brigandine: the legend of forsena","url":"https://presentationbuilder.internationaltrucks.com/brigandine-legend-forsena-2"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-17308"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena - Game Poster","url":"https://rpggamers.com/game/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena"},{"title":"🕹️ New release: Lunar Lander Beyond","url":"https://www.mobygames.com/game/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena"},{"title":"Brigandine the Legend of Forsena","url":"https://rawg.io/games/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena"},{"title":"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review","url":"https://turnbasedlovers.com/?p=28403"},{"title":"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena","url":"https://retro-replay.com/db/playstation/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena"},{"title":"Brigandine The Legend of Runersia – Pc Version – Review","url":"https://turnbasedlovers.com/review/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia-pc-version-review"},{"title":"brigandine the legend of forsena","url":"https://nextquest.dev/games/brigandine-the-legend-of-forsena"},{"title":"Brigandine (video game)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Brigandine_(video_game)"},{"title":"User Score","url":"https://legacy.prod.metacritic.com/game/switch/brigandine-the-legend-of-runersia/user-reviews"}]},"Reviews of Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (1998) mostly agree that the story is weak, though the setting and nations get some credit.\n\n- **Setting and premise:** One source describes a coup in the kingdom of Almekia that thrusts the continent of Forsena into war, with the player choosing one of six nations to conquer the rest. Brigandine invites you into the war-torn continent of Forsena, where the kingdom of Almekia has fallen to a ruthless coup.\n- **Named figures:** The RPGFan review lists rulers including Cai of Caerleon, Lance, Prince of New Almekia, Lyonesse of Leonia, and Vaynard of Norgard. Cai, the Silent and Wise King of Caerleon; Lance the Prince of New Almekia; Lyonesee, Queen of Leonia; Vaynard, ruler of Norgard and Dryst, the Mad Duke of Iscalio. I didn't find a source describing Zemeckis's role in detail. One RPGamer retroview says dark forces were behind urging Zemeckis's actions, but the true architect of the continent-wide conflict is never fully addressed even by the story's conclusion.\n- **Critical reception:** Reviewers are harsh. RPGFan calls the story extremely thin. Game Revolution's verdict is blunt, listing the story as absolutely pitiful. The RPGamer retroview lists \"perfunctory story\" among its cons. A Metacritic user says the Forsena story has more twists, turning points, and less pacing issue than its sequel's.\n- **Story delivery:** Story arrives through brief dialogue. Game Revolution notes that Brigandine's \"story\" consists of short sequences of dialogue that occasionally pop up after every turn on the world map.\n\nOverall, the consensus is that the gameplay carries the game and the story is secondary. Retro Replay is the one outlier, praising the game excels in its branching story paths. Sources are mixed on whether the story is a flaw or an acceptable backdrop."],"durationSeconds":6.244339373999974,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XU9Z9bFQjxCAao9JK79aof","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
