{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuaG5o5PyNNptt1oxwG4Pq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t3:Every public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n2\t28:const E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\n3\t29:const hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\n4\t39:const E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\n5\t70:- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n6\t221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n7\t223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n8\t270:- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), release(code), tap(action) and hold(action, on)\n9\t294:- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a dragon punch, '41236' a half circle. facing: 1 (right, the default) or -1. button: an action, 'attack+kick', or none (the motion alone)\n10\t303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n11\t385:- `new E.Particles(game) → game.particles` †: game.particles; game: its game\n12\t453:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause: true, id, pace, camera }). The standard features (section 10b) every game gets: menu, fullscreen, corner, backGesture, autoPause.\n13\t454:- `new E.Game({ res })`: a fixed resolution ('ps1' or [w, h]), whole pixels\n14\t455:- `new E.Game({ expand })`: true makes res the least the screen shows and grows the picture to fill the window, any shape, no bars (expand: { maxW, maxH } stops it growing there)\n15\t456:- `new E.Game({ bg })`: the color behind everything, or null: the canvas is clear, and the game draws its HUD and menus over a picture under it (a 3D world, engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js)\n16\t457:- `new E.Game({ headless })`: no screen, renderer, sound or DOM input (tests, tools, a simulation in Node, where it is the default): scenes update and draw is skipped; drive it with advance() and input.press / release / tap / hold\n17\t458:- `new E.Game({ loop })`: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\n18\t459:- `new E.Game({ menu })`: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\n19\t460:- `new E.Game({ fullscreen })`: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\n20\t461:- `new E.Game({ corner, backGesture })`: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\n21\t462:- `new E.Game({ autoPause })`: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n22\t463:- `new E.Game({ id })`: the name the player's settings are saved under (the page's path)\n23\t464:- `new E.Game({ pace })`: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\n24\t465:- `new E.Game({ camera })`: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\n25\t586:- `new E.Script(game, fn, o = {}) → script` †: a script, made by game.script: done (it returned, or was cancelled), value (what it returned), cancel(); another script can yield it\n26\t591:- `new E.Tween(game, target, to, seconds, o = {}) → tween` †: a tween, made by game.tween: done (it ended, or was cancelled), cancel(); a script can yield it\n27\t603:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; smooth: 'catmull' curves through every point (Catmull-Rom); at(d), nearest(x, y, z), draw(r) below\n28\t617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n29\t640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n30\t653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n31\t666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair)\n32\t703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n33\t713:- `new E.Blob(o = {}) → blob`: new E.Blob({ R: 6.5, colors, ears, horns, wings, feet, tail, mouth, face }): a squash-and-stretch rig for slimes and jellies; blob.update(dt, state) each step, blob.draw(g, ox, oy, view) in an r.actor\n34\t714:- `blob.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw(g, ox, oy, view). Creature features from the constructor options: ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true (flapping bat wings), feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' (eyes always on the camera side, for Mana-style monsters) update(dt, { flap: 0..1, hang: true }) slows or folds the wings and hangs a bat upside down from its anchor.\n35\t733:- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], types, floorTex } (built in code: fill, setFloor; with no cells it starts as open floor).\n36\t734:- `new E.TileMap({ types })`: types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH, face, roof }\n37\t735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n38\t736:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n39\t737:- `new E.TileMap({ floorTex })`: floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view) -> [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, glow]\n40\t738:- `new E.TileMap({ floorMat, floorMats })`: a material for the floor, floorMats: { tag: material } for tagged cells (in place of floorTex)\n41\t739:- `new E.TileMap({ block })`: ['water', 'lava'] floor tags nobody can walk on (or put block: true in a legend entry)\n42\t740:- `new E.TileMap({ chunks })`: bake the floor in squares near the camera (true, false; by default a map of more than 128 x 128 cells)\n43\t817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n44\t818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n45\t819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n46\t846:- `new E.PlatformMap(o = {}) → level`: { rows: [...ASCII, top row first...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types: { 1: {...} }, tile: 16, depth: 16 }. Tile kinds: 'solid' (default) | 'oneway' | 'ladder' | 'slope' | 'hazard' | 'deco' | 'back'\n47\t880:- `new E.Platformer(o = {}) → hero`: a side-scroller character body with modern, forgiving controls (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, optional double jump, wall jump, dash, ladders, knockback). const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22 }); update: hero.update(dt, level, game.input) (or an intent object for enemies: { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }) then read hero.onGround, hero.jumped, hero.landed, hero.facing (1 or -1), hero.climbing, hero.air draw a Humanoid with rig.update(dt, hero.rigState()) Units: world units per second. One tile = 16. A 285 jump with gravity 800 clears about 3 tiles.\n48\t921:- `new E.Body(o = {}) → body`: new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, ... })\n49\t942:- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n50\t963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n51\t1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds. Each step: suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)\n52\t1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n53\t1039:- `new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32) → grid`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply; map: the buckets\n54\t1045:- `grid.cell`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply. cell: the bucket size in world units; map: the buckets\n55\t1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n56\t1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n57\t1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n58\t1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n59\t1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n60\t1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n61\t1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n62\t1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n63\t1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n64\t1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n65\t1257:- `new E.Click(game, o = {}) → click` †: new E.Click(game, { rooms, items, rules, hero, ui, story, room, at, on }): see the manual\n66\t1290:- `new E.Walkbox(outline, holes = []) → walkbox` †: new E.Walkbox(outline, holes): polygons of [x, y] (room pixels); holes are places inside it no one stands\n67\t1302:- `new E.Car(o = {}) → car`: new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n68\t1321:- `new E.Race(o = {}) → race`: new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual)\n69\t1341:- `new E.FightAI(o = {}) → fightai` †: new E.FightAI({ level: 1..8 (4), seed }): a CPU for a fighter\n70\t1346:- `new E.FightSelect(game, o = {}) → fightselect` †: new E.FightSelect(game, { roster: [{ id, name, rig, about }], inputs: [p1, p2 or null], cpu: [false, true], seed, onDone: ids => {} }): a character select\n71\t1358:- `new E.FightStage(x0 = 0, x1 = 520) → fightstage` †: new E.FightStage(x0, x1): a flat floor at z 0\n72\t1364:- `new E.Fighter(game, o = {}) → fighter` †: new E.Fighter(game, { name, x, side: 1 (faces right), rig: Humanoid options (or a Humanoid), life: 1000, walk: 75, back: 60, jump: 390, jumpX: 90, moves, throwBtn: 'hp', throwRange, throwDmg: 120, input })\n73\t1401:- `new E.Match(game, o = {}) → match` †: new E.Match(game, { fighters: [a, b], ai: [null, null] (E.FightAI each, or null for its input), inputs: [game. input, null], rounds: 2 (wins needed), time: 99, x0: 0, x1: 520, span: 250 (how far apart they may be), camera: true (the game's camera follows them), training: false | { dummy }, onEnd: winner => {} })\n74\t1432:- `new E.Fog(grid) → fog`: new E.Fog(grid): every cell unseen; update() with the viewers each turn\n75\t1439:- `new E.Grid(w, h, o = {}) → grid`: new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: false | 'pointy' | 'flat', walkable(cx, cy), cost(cx, cy), height(cx, cy), opaque(cx, cy), diagonal }): w x h cells, every one walkable at cost 1 and height 0 unless the functions say otherwise\n76\t1464:- `new E.GridMover(o = {}) → gridmover`: new E.GridMover({ cx, cy, speed: 6 (cells a second) })\n77\t1473:- `new E.Turns(actors = [], o = {}) → turns`: new E.Turns(actors, { mode: 'speed' | 'ct' | 'phase' | 'atb', sides: ['hero', 'foe'] (phase), fill: 1 (atb: gauge per second at speed 100) }). An actor is any object with speed (100: normal) and, in phase mode, side\n78\t1514:- `new E.Physics(o = {}) → physics`: new E.Physics({ gravity, substeps, iterations, sleep, on, cell }): a world of bodies (see the manual)\n79\t1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n80\t1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n81\t----\n82\t5:## Units and the height rules\n83\t22:## Examples\n84\t47:## Contents\n85\t108:## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n86\t119:## 1. Math\n87\t194:## 2. Pixel primitives\n88\t213:## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n89\t219:## 3. Views (projections)\n90\t246:## 4. Screen\n91\t268:## 5. Input\n92\t353:## 6. Pixel font\n93\t364:## 7. Lighting\n94\t383:## 8. Particles\n95\t403:## 9. Renderer\n96\t451:## 10. Game\n97\t562:## 10b. Standard features\n98\t579:## 10c. Boot\n99\t584:## 10d. Tweens and scripts\n100\t601:## 10e. Paths\n101\t611:## 10g. Weather\n102\t615:## 10k. Save slots\n103\t638:## 11. Humanoid rig\n104\t711:## 12. Blob rig\n105\t731:## 13. Tile map\n106\t794:## 13b. Materials\n107\t815:## 14. Flow field\n108\t833:## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n109\t844:## 16. Platform map\n110\t878:## 16b. Platformer\n111\t919:## 17. Body\n112\t939:## 17b. Actions\n113\t961:## 17c. Mover\n114\t1000:## 17d. Perception\n115\t1017:## 18. Bullets\n116\t1037:## 19. Spatial hash\n117\t1047:## 20. Audio\n118\t1079:## 21b. Backdrops\n119\t1087:## 21c. Props\n120\t1092:## 21e. Shapes\n121\t1104:## 21. Ui\n122\t1161:## 21d. Shell\n123\t1190:## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\n124\t1211:## 23. Sessions\n125\t1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n126\t1255:## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)\n127\t1300:## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n128\t1338:## Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js)\n129\t1419:## Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed (engine/modules/gen.js)\n130\t1430:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js)\n131\t1489:## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js)\n132\t1512:## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js)\n133\t1541:## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\n134\t1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n135\t1590:## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)\n136\t1619:## Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters (engine/modules/rpg.js)\n137\t1638:## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\n138\t1646:## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js)\n139\t1675:## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js)\n140\t1721:## Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js)\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"530f1c16-e781-4b8b-8ed6-4454282908ae","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:54:58.659Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/out12.txt","content":"3:Every public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n28:const E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\n29:const hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\n39:const E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\n70:- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n270:- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), release(code), tap(action) and hold(action, on)\n294:- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a dragon punch, '41236' a half circle. facing: 1 (right, the default) or -1. button: an action, 'attack+kick', or none (the motion alone)\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n385:- `new E.Particles(game) → game.particles` †: game.particles; game: its game\n453:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause: true, id, pace, camera }). The standard features (section 10b) every game gets: menu, fullscreen, corner, backGesture, autoPause.\n454:- `new E.Game({ res })`: a fixed resolution ('ps1' or [w, h]), whole pixels\n455:- `new E.Game({ expand })`: true makes res the least the screen shows and grows the picture to fill the window, any shape, no bars (expand: { maxW, maxH } stops it growing there)\n456:- `new E.Game({ bg })`: the color behind everything, or null: the canvas is clear, and the game draws its HUD and menus over a picture under it (a 3D world, engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js)\n457:- `new E.Game({ headless })`: no screen, renderer, sound or DOM input (tests, tools, a simulation in Node, where it is the default): scenes update and draw is skipped; drive it with advance() and input.press / release / tap / hold\n458:- `new E.Game({ loop })`: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\n459:- `new E.Game({ menu })`: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\n460:- `new E.Game({ fullscreen })`: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\n461:- `new E.Game({ corner, backGesture })`: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\n462:- `new E.Game({ autoPause })`: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n463:- `new E.Game({ id })`: the name the player's settings are saved under (the page's path)\n464:- `new E.Game({ pace })`: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\n465:- `new E.Game({ camera })`: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\n586:- `new E.Script(game, fn, o = {}) → script` †: a script, made by game.script: done (it returned, or was cancelled), value (what it returned), cancel(); another script can yield it\n591:- `new E.Tween(game, target, to, seconds, o = {}) → tween` †: a tween, made by game.tween: done (it ended, or was cancelled), cancel(); a script can yield it\n603:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; smooth: 'catmull' curves through every point (Catmull-Rom); at(d), nearest(x, y, z), draw(r) below\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair)\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n713:- `new E.Blob(o = {}) → blob`: new E.Blob({ R: 6.5, colors, ears, horns, wings, feet, tail, mouth, face }): a squash-and-stretch rig for slimes and jellies; blob.update(dt, state) each step, blob.draw(g, ox, oy, view) in an r.actor\n714:- `blob.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw(g, ox, oy, view). Creature features from the constructor options: ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true (flapping bat wings), feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' (eyes always on the camera side, for Mana-style monsters) update(dt, { flap: 0..1, hang: true }) slows or folds the wings and hangs a bat upside down from its anchor.\n733:- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], types, floorTex } (built in code: fill, setFloor; with no cells it starts as open floor).\n734:- `new E.TileMap({ types })`: types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH, face, roof }\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n736:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n737:- `new E.TileMap({ floorTex })`: floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view) -> [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, glow]\n738:- `new E.TileMap({ floorMat, floorMats })`: a material for the floor, floorMats: { tag: material } for tagged cells (in place of floorTex)\n739:- `new E.TileMap({ block })`: ['water', 'lava'] floor tags nobody can walk on (or put block: true in a legend entry)\n740:- `new E.TileMap({ chunks })`: bake the floor in squares near the camera (true, false; by default a map of more than 128 x 128 cells)\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n846:- `new E.PlatformMap(o = {}) → level`: { rows: [...ASCII, top row first...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types: { 1: {...} }, tile: 16, depth: 16 }. Tile kinds: 'solid' (default) | 'oneway' | 'ladder' | 'slope' | 'hazard' | 'deco' | 'back'\n880:- `new E.Platformer(o = {}) → hero`: a side-scroller character body with modern, forgiving controls (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, optional double jump, wall jump, dash, ladders, knockback). const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22 }); update: hero.update(dt, level, game.input) (or an intent object for enemies: { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }) then read hero.onGround, hero.jumped, hero.landed, hero.facing (1 or -1), hero.climbing, hero.air draw a Humanoid with rig.update(dt, hero.rigState()) Units: world units per second. One tile = 16. A 285 jump with gravity 800 clears about 3 tiles.\n921:- `new E.Body(o = {}) → body`: new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, ... })\n942:- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds. Each step: suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)\n1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n1039:- `new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32) → grid`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply; map: the buckets\n1045:- `grid.cell`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply. cell: the bucket size in world units; map: the buckets\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1257:- `new E.Click(game, o = {}) → click` †: new E.Click(game, { rooms, items, rules, hero, ui, story, room, at, on }): see the manual\n1290:- `new E.Walkbox(outline, holes = []) → walkbox` †: new E.Walkbox(outline, holes): polygons of [x, y] (room pixels); holes are places inside it no one stands\n1302:- `new E.Car(o = {}) → car`: new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n1321:- `new E.Race(o = {}) → race`: new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual)\n1341:- `new E.FightAI(o = {}) → fightai` †: new E.FightAI({ level: 1..8 (4), seed }): a CPU for a fighter\n1346:- `new E.FightSelect(game, o = {}) → fightselect` †: new E.FightSelect(game, { roster: [{ id, name, rig, about }], inputs: [p1, p2 or null], cpu: [false, true], seed, onDone: ids => {} }): a character select\n1358:- `new E.FightStage(x0 = 0, x1 = 520) → fightstage` †: new E.FightStage(x0, x1): a flat floor at z 0\n1364:- `new E.Fighter(game, o = {}) → fighter` †: new E.Fighter(game, { name, x, side: 1 (faces right), rig: Humanoid options (or a Humanoid), life: 1000, walk: 75, back: 60, jump: 390, jumpX: 90, moves, throwBtn: 'hp', throwRange, throwDmg: 120, input })\n1401:- `new E.Match(game, o = {}) → match` †: new E.Match(game, { fighters: [a, b], ai: [null, null] (E.FightAI each, or null for its input), inputs: [game. input, null], rounds: 2 (wins needed), time: 99, x0: 0, x1: 520, span: 250 (how far apart they may be), camera: true (the game's camera follows them), training: false | { dummy }, onEnd: winner => {} })\n1432:- `new E.Fog(grid) → fog`: new E.Fog(grid): every cell unseen; update() with the viewers each turn\n1439:- `new E.Grid(w, h, o = {}) → grid`: new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: false | 'pointy' | 'flat', walkable(cx, cy), cost(cx, cy), height(cx, cy), opaque(cx, cy), diagonal }): w x h cells, every one walkable at cost 1 and height 0 unless the functions say otherwise\n1464:- `new E.GridMover(o = {}) → gridmover`: new E.GridMover({ cx, cy, speed: 6 (cells a second) })\n1473:- `new E.Turns(actors = [], o = {}) → turns`: new E.Turns(actors, { mode: 'speed' | 'ct' | 'phase' | 'atb', sides: ['hero', 'foe'] (phase), fill: 1 (atb: gauge per second at speed 100) }). An actor is any object with speed (100: normal) and, in phase mode, side\n1514:- `new E.Physics(o = {}) → physics`: new E.Physics({ gravity, substeps, iterations, sleep, on, cell }): a world of bodies (see the manual)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n----\n5:## Units and the height rules\n22:## Examples\n47:## Contents\n108:## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n119:## 1. Math\n194:## 2. Pixel primitives\n213:## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n219:## 3. Views (projections)\n246:## 4. Screen\n268:## 5. Input\n353:## 6. Pixel font\n364:## 7. Lighting\n383:## 8. Particles\n403:## 9. Renderer\n451:## 10. Game\n562:## 10b. Standard features\n579:## 10c. Boot\n584:## 10d. Tweens and scripts\n601:## 10e. Paths\n611:## 10g. Weather\n615:## 10k. Save slots\n638:## 11. Humanoid rig\n711:## 12. Blob rig\n731:## 13. Tile map\n794:## 13b. Materials\n815:## 14. Flow field\n833:## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n844:## 16. Platform map\n878:## 16b. Platformer\n919:## 17. Body\n939:## 17b. Actions\n961:## 17c. Mover\n1000:## 17d. Perception\n1017:## 18. Bullets\n1037:## 19. Spatial hash\n1047:## 20. Audio\n1079:## 21b. Backdrops\n1087:## 21c. Props\n1092:## 21e. Shapes\n1104:## 21. Ui\n1161:## 21d. Shell\n1190:## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\n1211:## 23. Sessions\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1255:## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)\n1300:## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n1338:## Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js)\n1419:## Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed (engine/modules/gen.js)\n1430:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js)\n1489:## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js)\n1512:## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js)\n1541:## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1590:## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)\n1619:## Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters (engine/modules/rpg.js)\n1638:## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\n1646:## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js)\n1675:## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, f