{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GVNm7Jv2UZrRA9JdZUtVKp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 21. Ui\n2\t\n3\t- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n4\t- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n5\t- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n6\t- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n7\t- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n8\t- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom', y, alpha, vars: the values {$name} reads } choices: ['YES', 'NO'], shown on the last page (picked by the keys, or a tap or click on one); onChoice(i) gets the one picked. update(dt) returns true while a modal box is open: return from your update then, and play waits\n9\t- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n10\t- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n11\t- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n12\t- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n13\t- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n14\t- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n15\t- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n16\t- `talk.game`: its game\n17\t- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n18\t- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n19\t- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n20\t- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n21\t- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n22\t- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n23\t- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n24\t- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n25\t- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n26\t- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n27\t- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n28\t- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n29\t- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n30\t- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n31\t- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n32\t- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n33\t- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n34\t- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n35\t- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n36\t- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n37\t- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n38\t- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n39\t- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n40\t- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n41\t- `menu.game`: its game\n42\t- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n43\t- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n44\t- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n45\t- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n46\t- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n47\t- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n48\t- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n49\t- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n50\t- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n51\t- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n52\t- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n53\t- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n54\t- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n55\t- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n56\t- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n57\t\n58\t----\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"11deb7c0-12ad-48fa-acf4-834512bc0c5c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:01:30.143Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research/out15.txt","content":"## 21. Ui\n\n- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom', y, alpha, vars: the values {$name} reads } choices: ['YES', 'NO'], shown on the last page (picked by the keys, or a tap or click on one); onChoice(i) gets the one picked. update(dt) returns true while a modal box is open: return from your update then, and play waits\n- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n- `talk.game`: its game\n- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n- `menu.game`: its game\n- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n\n----\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GVNm7Jv2UZrRA9JdZUtVKp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
