{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2eSekMngZDeqxwTg5D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Part 3 is in; I'm appending the 13 validated battle maps from the checked generator output next, then the quest sites and story.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33582,"cache_read_input_tokens":452372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33582},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"b5a5add4-c6e1-42d9-85ad-6989a6142df7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:04.188Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2eSPsJEK7U5V6neko4","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2eSekMngZDeqxwTg5D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DXTMcZfKUjRmHoGTLvJ74f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF' > maps_md.txt 2>&1\nsrc = open('scripts/maps.py').read()\n# run the generator without its printing tail, then format the maps as markdown\nhead = src.split(\"bad = 0\")[0]\nns = {}\nexec(compile(head, 'maps.py', 'exec'), ns)\nmaps = ns['maps']; validate = ns['validate']\nnotes = {\n 'border_meadow': ('Border Meadow', 'the tutorial (§6.13) and Skirmish', 'A meadow with a stream, a bridge on the road and a ruined watchtower Keep. Two troops a side: anchors 1 2 against 7 8.'),\n 'river_ford': ('River Ford', 'Rainmere, Thawgate', 'A river splits the field, with two fords and one bridge on the road. In Spring the fords flood and only the bridge crosses; in Winter the river freezes into open ground.'),\n 'forest_hold': ('Forest Hold', 'Kestrel Spire, Thornwick, Lanternfall', 'Thick woods, a winding road and a clearing Keep between two hills. Forest slows large units (cost 3); in Summer fire can burn it open.'),\n 'mountain_pass': ('Mountain Pass', 'Wolfsgate, Cinderwall', 'Peaks squeeze the field into a pass 3 to 5 hexes wide, with ruins in it. Fliers cross the peaks. The Keep holds the pass\\'s mouth.'),\n 'hill_fort': ('Hill Fort', 'Midnight Keep, Dawnwatch, Lionsreach', 'The Keep crowns a ring of hills (+10% DEF, +1 range for bows) with woods on both flanks.'),\n 'marsh_keep': ('Marsh Keep', 'Russetmoor, Beltane Ford', 'Bogs and pools around a causeway road. Summer dries the swamp; Spring floods the pools.'),\n 'lakeside': ('Lakeside', 'Frostmere, Primrose Ford', 'A lake fills the north and the land route bends south around it. In Winter the lake freezes and opens a straight path to the Keep.'),\n 'ruined_abbey': ('Ruined Abbey', 'Vesper Hall, Ashbarrow, Hallowmere', 'Broken walls (blocked) and ruins (+10% DEF) around an abbey-tower Keep.'),\n 'crossroads': ('Crossroads', 'Noonspire, Goldspur, Lammas Cross', 'Two roads cross among fields, with houses (blocked) making lanes. Summer wheat hides units (+10 evade).'),\n 'capital_citadel': ('Capital Citadel', 'Rimeholt, Avalorn, Brazenhold, Ambergate', 'A ring of ramparts round the courtyard and Keep, with a west gate on the road and a south-west gate. Fliers cross the walls; walkers must use a gate. Dressing follows the realm (ice, blossom, sandstone, timber).'),\n 'meridian_clockyard': ('Meridian Clockyard', 'Meridian', 'The clock-city: an outer wall with three gates, gear blocks inside, and the Great Clock tower as the Keep.'),\n 'clockwork_sanctum': ('Clockwork Sanctum', 'the final battle', 'A round dial chamber. The Gray Knight\\'s troop starts at the centre (7 8 9) and the player\\'s troops enter from the south (1 2 3). Season Dials D stand at north, east, south and west. Its rules follow the map.'),\n 'wheel_shrine': ('Wheel Shrine', 'Skirmish and the AI Hub', 'Four corners, seats 1 to 4 (Spring NE, Summer SE, Autumn SW, Winter NW), around the Hour Shrine (K) in its courtyard. With 2 sides use seats 1 and 3; with 3 sides use 1, 2 and 3.'),\n}\norder = ['border_meadow','river_ford','forest_hold','mountain_pass','hill_fort','marsh_keep','lakeside','ruined_abbey','crossroads','capital_citadel','meridian_clockyard','clockwork_sanctum','wheel_shrine']\nout = []\nout.append('### 6.10 Battle maps (13)')\nout.append('Each map is a list of rows, top row first, one character per hex (codes in §5.7; anchors `1 2 3` attacker, `7 8 9` defender, `1 2 3 4` seats). Odd rows sit half a hex to the right. A script built and checked every map below: every row has the same length; each anchor appears once and has at least 7 free hexes within 2 steps; and the Keep can be reached from every attacker anchor in all four seasons, floods and ice included. Keep that check as a test (§14). `flood` marks maps whose shallows flood in Spring.')\nout.append('')\nfor k in order:\n    name, used, note = notes[k]\n    rows = maps[k]['rows']\n    two = k == 'border_meadow'\n    errs = validate(k, rows, flood=maps[k]['flood'], seats=maps[k].get('seats'), attackers='12' if two else '123', defenders='78' if two else '789')\n    assert not errs, (k, errs)\n    out.append(f'**{name}** (`{k}`, {len(rows[0])} × {len(rows)}{\", flood\" if maps[k][\"flood\"] else \"\"}): used by {used}. {note}')\n    out.append('```')\n    out.extend(rows)\n    out.append('```')\nout.append('')\nout.append('**Clockwork Sanctum rules (the final battle):**')\nout.append('- The player wins when the Gray Knight falls; that is the ruler rule. If he stands at the end of bell 12, the thirteenth bell tolls and the battle is lost (§4.17).')\nout.append('- **The Hour Hand:** at the end of each bell it points along one of the 6 hex directions from the centre, moving one step clockwise per bell. Every player unit on that `line6` (to the wall) rolls Stop 70. The next bell\\'s line glows faintly all bell long, so players can step aside.')\nout.append('- **Season Dials (`D`):** at the end of a bell, a dial with a player unit on it lights and stays lit. A Dominion unit standing on a lit dial at a bell\\'s end puts it out. When all four are lit at once, \"The Wheel turns!\": Timeless breaks for the rest of the battle (full damage, effects apply), the Gray Knight\\'s DEF drops 40%, and the Hour Hand stops.')\nout.append('- **At 50% HP** the Gray Knight calls 2 Second Hands (tier-3 Minutes, level 20). They head for lit dials, and he uses Still every 2 bells instead of every 3.')\nout.append('- **Lunete (if she is present):** her Turning (×2 against Hour) breaks Timeless for one bell, and a dial she stands on lights at once instead of at the bell\\'s end.')\nout.append('- The troops that took Meridian enter, healed to full (\"the Wheel\\'s light\"), plus up to one more troop from a castle adjacent to Meridian.')\nout.append('')\nout.append('**Wheel Shrine rules (Skirmish \"Banners of the Wheel\" and the AI Hub):**')\nout.append('- A free-for-all of 2 to 4 sides, one troop each (a ruler at level 10 with 2 monsters, §11.4), lasting 6 bells.')\nout.append('- **The season turns every bell:** bell 1 Spring, 2 Summer, 3 Autumn, 4 Winter, 5 Spring, 6 Summer. The Tide and terrain transforms are applied again at each bell\\'s start.')\nout.append('- **Glory:** +1 for every 5 damage dealt, +10 per monster KO, +25 per knight KO, +5 at each bell\\'s end for the side holding the Shrine (`K`), and +10 at the end if your knight still stands.')\nout.append('- Highest glory wins; ties share a place. A knight that falls takes its troop out, but its glory still counts.')\nprint('\\n'.join(out))\nEOF\ntail -5 maps_md.txt; wc -l maps_md.txt","description":"Generate the battle map section in markdown from checked data"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33582,"cache_read_input_tokens":452372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33582},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"75eed7b1-3c0a-4b2d-92ef-d95bacc7453d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:28.463Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2eSPsJEK7U5V6neko4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DXTMcZfKUjRmHoGTLvJ74f":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/.research && python3 -I - <<'EOF' > maps_md.txt 2>&1\nsrc = open('scripts/maps.py').read()\n# run the generator without its printing tail, then format the maps as markdown\nhead = src.split(\"bad = 0\")[0]\nns = {}\nexec(compile(head, 'maps.py', 'exec'), ns)\nmaps = ns['maps']; validate = ns['validate']\nnotes = {\n 'border_meadow': ('Border Meado