{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3kuZXuMGcgwsE37Y2v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found three small issues so far (the end-phase key says Backspace but §8.2 uses Space; a leftover `mirror` field; \"five\" castle styles where §7.3 lists six). I'll note them and keep reading."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11720,"cache_read_input_tokens":570809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11720},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"56dd82fc-38fb-4ded-9046-2d99585d371c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:49:52.797Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3kuGfMThGVRX2sc6Fi"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3kuZXuMGcgwsE37Y2v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DU8M8Jv6bBpyFUeLr6MouS","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11720,"cache_read_input_tokens":570809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11720},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"ee286fd6-2dd8-4c16-8c7d-21f4f0d56505","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:49:54.105Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3kuGfMThGVRX2sc6Fi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DU8M8Jv6bBpyFUeLr6MouS":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DU8M8Jv6bBpyFUeLr6MouS","type":"tool_result","content":"330\t- **Who:** any knight who is not a ruler, not wounded and has not moved this Muster. It leaves with its troop for the\n331\t  site's duration (1 or 2 seasons). At most 2 knights per realm may be away at once.\n332\t- **The outcome is rolled at departure** (seeded) and revealed in a vignette when the knight returns. Base weights:\n333\t\n334\t| Outcome | Weight | Effect |\n335\t|---|---|---|\n336\t| Treasure | 30 | an item from the site's pool |\n337\t| Beast | 20 | a monster from the site's pool joins the troop (or the castle reserve), at level = knight level − 2 |\n338\t| Wanderer | 10 (0 if none is free) | a free knight from the site's region joins (§6.5.6) |\n339\t| Mana spring | 15 | +40 to +80 mana |\n340\t| Training | 15 | +60 EXP for the knight, +40 for each monster in its troop |\n341\t| Mishap | 10 | the knight returns wounded (out 1 season); 30% chance its weakest monster is lost |\n342\t\n343\t- **Modifiers:** Cleric line +10 Treasure; Beast line +15 Beast; Ranger line +10 Wanderer; knight level 10 or more:\n344\t  Mishap −5; the Lucky Horseshoe multiplies the four good outcomes by 1.15; a site's focus adds +10 to its outcome (§6.11).\n345\t  Story sites override the table (§6.12).\n346\t\n347\t### 4.10 Equip and items\n348\t- Items sit in one inventory per realm. A knight has three slots: weapon, armor and accessory.\n349\t- Each class line allows certain weapon kinds: Warrior (sword, spear, axe), Ranger (bow), Mage (staff, tome), Cleric\n350\t  (staff, mace), Beast (whip, spear); rulers per class (§6.6).\n351\t- Consumables can be used during Muster on any unit at the same castle. They can also be used in battle by knights\n352\t  (the Item action, §5.4), from the realm inventory.\n353\t\n354\t### 4.11 Promotions and class changes (Muster only, with an animation and a jingle)\n355\t- **Monsters:** tier 2 at level 12, or with the matching Season Seed from level 6; tier 3 at level 22, or with a Seed\n356\t  from level 16. Hour monsters promote by level only. The level stays, the new form's base stats apply, and the bond\n357\t  cost does not change.\n358\t- **Knights:** tier 2 at level 10 (free); tier 3 at level 20 plus a Writ of Knighthood. At the change every stat is\n359\t  multiplied by 1.10 (§6.6).\n360\t\n361\t### 4.12 Declaring a march\n362\t- Pick an enemy or neutral castle adjacent to at least one of yours, then up to 3 knights (each with its troop) from your\n363\t  castles adjacent to the target.\n364\t- Wounded, questing or Stilled knights can't march, and each knight marches at most once a season.\n365\t- Several attacks per season are allowed, one per target.\n366\t- A castle you leave with no knights is open: an enemy attack on it takes it without a battle.\n367\t- Arrows on the map show every declaration (the AI's appear at resolution).\n368\t\n369\t### 4.13 Resolution\n370\t1. Sort every declared attack by the attacker's highest knight level (descending), then by attacking power, then by a\n371\t   seeded tie-break.\n372\t2. For each attack in turn:\n373\t   - If the target already belongs to the attacker, or every attacking troop is gone, skip it.\n374\t   - If the target holds no knights, it changes hands (\"The gates stand open\").\n375\t   - Otherwise there is a battle. If a human commands either side, ask **Command** (fight it) or **Delegate**\n376\t     (auto-resolve, §5.14); otherwise auto-resolve.\n377\t3. Apply the aftermath (§4.14) after each battle, before the next one. Units keep their damage until the next Tidings,\n378\t   so a castle attacked twice in one season fights the second battle hurt.\n379\t\n380\t### 4.14 Aftermath\n381\t- **If the attacker wins:** the castle changes owner and the attacking troops occupy it.\n382\t  - Surviving or retreated defending knights fall back to the nearest castle of their realm, by roads. If that castle\n383\t    is not adjacent, they still go there. If the realm has no castle, it is eliminated.\n384\t  - Unbound monsters in the castle's reserve join the new owner's reserve.\n385\t  - The first time a castle is taken, its treasury item goes to the winner.\n386\t  - A brigand castle taken by a human triggers `brigands_no_more` (§6.12).\n387\t- **If the defender wins:** the attacking troops go home to the castles they came from.\n388\t- **Losses:** knights at 0 HP are wounded (they miss the next season: no move, march or quest, but they can be\n389\t  organized). Monsters at 0 HP are dead. Captures follow §5.9. A ruler at 0 HP or retreating loses the battle for its\n390\t  side.\n391\t- **Elimination:** a realm with no castles is out. Its knights become free and join the wanderer pools of their old\n392\t  regions; its ruler goes into exile. If it was the player's only realm, the game is lost (in hot-seat, that human\n393\t  watches until the game ends).\n394\t\n395\t### 4.15 Campaign AI (`23-ai-campaign.js`, deterministic per seed)\n396\t- **Power:** `power(unit) = (HP + 4 × (ATK + DEF + INT) + 2 × AGI) × (1 + 0.05 × (level − 1))`, ×1.2 for knights. A\n397\t  troop's power is the sum over its units. `defense(c)` = the power of the troops at c × 1.25 (the Keep).\n398\t- **Threat:** `threat(c)` = Σ over adjacent castles of other season-realms (and of the Dominion once it is active) of\n399\t  their marchable power × that realm's aggression (×1.2 in its own season). `need(c) = threat(c) − defense(c)`.\n400\t- **Muster, in order:**\n401\t  1. **Summon** while mana > 1.5 × upkeep + 40. Pick the castle with the highest need. Score each option by power per\n402\t     mana × 1.2 if its element opposes the strongest neighbouring realm's element, × 1.1 if its element is next\n403\t     season's. Bind the monster to a knight there with free Bond, or keep it in reserve.\n404\t  2. **Bind** reserve monsters to knights with free Bond, strongest first.\n405\t  3. **Move** up to 3 troops, each from the castle with the most surplus to an adjacent castle with the highest need.\n406\t     Never leave a border castle (one adjacent to a foe) without a knight.\n407\t  4. **Quest** with knights at interior castles that have no need (at most 2 away), at the site with the best expected\n408\t     value.\n409\t  5. **Equip** the best item per slot (ATK for warriors, rangers and tamers; INT for mages and clerics; armor by DEF;\n410\t     accessories by Bond, then Spurs, then Ward). **Promote** and class-change whenever eligible.\n411\t- **March:**\n412\t  - For each adjacent foreign castle, the attackers are troops that are not needed at home. A troop is needed if taking\n413\t    it leaves `need(c) > 0.4 × threat(c)` or leaves a border castle empty.\n414\t  - `ratio = Σ top-3 attacker power / defense(target)` (an empty castle is ∞). Attack if `ratio ≥ threshold /\n415\t    aggression`, where threshold is 1.6 / 1.3 / 1.1 on Easy / Normal / Hard.\n416\t  - Target value: Meridian ×1.5 (if the realm holds an adjacent satellite), capitals ×1.3, brigand castles ×1.2 in Year\n417\t    1; then the highest ratio. Each troop marches once.\n418\t- **Personalities:**\n419\t\n420\t| Realm | Aggression | Quirk |\n421\t|---|---|---|\n422\t| Solmark | 1.15 | ×1.3 in Summer; prefers the weakest neighbour |\n423\t| Hoarfast | rolled each season between 0.9 and 1.4 (\"the Duke's moods\") | ×1.3 in Winter |\n424\t| Amberlyn | 0.85 | sends up to 3 questers; keeps one extra troop at its capital |\n425\t| Verdance | 1.0 | takes brigand castles first |\n426\t| Hourless Dominion | 0 in Year 1, 0.8 in Year 2, 1.1 from Year 3 | never leaves Meridian with fewer than 2 troops; summons only Hour monsters |\n427\t| Brigands | 0 | never march or summon; full HP at each Tidings |\n428\t\n429\t### 4.16 Stillness\n430\tFrom Autumn of Year 3, each Tidings the Gray Knight stills one castle (seeded) that borders Dominion territory, other\n431\tthan Meridian. For that season it yields no mana, and its troops can't move, march or quest (they defend normally). It\n432\tis drawn in grey with a stopped-clock icon. The first time, the `stillness` event plays; after that a toast announces it.\n433\t\n434\t### 4.17 Winning and losing\n435\t- **Win:** defeat the Gray Knight in the Clockwork Sanctum. That battle becomes available the moment your realm takes\n436\t  Meridian (§6.12, `meridian_falls`). If you lose it, your troops fall back into Meridian, and you can attack the\n437\t  Sanctum again from Meridian in a later March (the Sanctum shows as a special target beside Meridian).\n438\t- **Lose:**\n439\t  - your realm loses its last castle;\n440\t  - the candle burns out;\n441\t  - or a rival realm holds Meridian and wins its Sanctum battle. When an AI realm takes Meridian, it fights the Sanctum,\n442\t    auto-resolved, at the next Tidings. If it wins, it \"sets the Wheel\" to its season and you lose (a rival's bad\n443\t    ending). If it loses, Meridian returns to the Dominion with a fresh garrison (2 troops, level 14).\n444\t- **Hot-seat:** the first human to win wins for everyone; the others see their own epilogue card.\n445\t\n446\t### 4.18 Difficulty (chosen for each new campaign)\n447\t\n448\t| | Easy | Normal | Hard |\n449\t|---|---|---|---|\n450\t| AI mana income | ×0.8 | ×1.0 | ×1.25 |\n451\t| AI march threshold | 1.6 | 1.3 | 1.1 |\n452\t| Candle seasons | 16 | 12 | 10 |\n453\t| Enemy battle AI | picks from its top 3, weighted | the best plan | the best plan, plus focus fire |\n454\t| Player EXP | ×1.25 | ×1.0 | ×1.0 |\n455\t\n456\t---\n457\t\n458\t## 5. Battle rules (`BattleSim`)\n459\t\n460\t### 5.1 The field\n461\t- Pointy-top hexes in offset rows (odd rows shifted right): `new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: 'pointy', walkable, cost })`.\n462\t- A hex is `T = 28` world units across the flats; `grid.center(c, 28)` gives its centre.\n463\t- Maps run from 13 × 9 to 17 × 13 hexes, with one unit per hex.\n464\t- The field is flat (z = 0). Height comes from terrain types and props, as in the source's flat hex maps. Raised blocks\n465\t  (ramparts, gears, cliffs) are impassable shapes (§7.2).\n466\t\n467\t### 5.2 Sides and deployment\n468\t- Two sides, attacker and defender, each with up to 3 troops. A troop is one knight and up to 6 monsters.\n469\t- Troop anchors are hexes `1 2 3` (attacker) and `7 8 9` (defender). The defender's first troop takes the anchor next to\n470\t  the Keep. Skirmish and hub maps use seat anchors `1 2 3 4`.\n471\t- The knight stands on the anchor, and its monsters fill the free hexes nearest it according to its formation:\n472\t  - **Vanguard:** hexes 1–2 steps toward the enemy's side first.\n473\t  - **Shield:** the ring around the knight first.\n474\t  - **Column:** a line behind the knight, away from the enemy.\n475\t- Units face the enemy side.\n476\t\n477\t### 5.3 Bells and turn order\n478\t- A battle lasts up to `tune.bells` (12) bells.\n479\t- Each bell, troops act in order of their knight's AGI (descending; ties go to the defender, then the lower troop id).\n480\t- In a troop's turn, each of its units acts once, in any order its controller likes. The troop ends when all have acted\n481\t  or its controller ends it (the rest Wait). A troop whose knight has fallen is gone.\n482\t- **At the end of each bell:**\n483\t  1. effects tick (§5.8);\n484\t  2. the Keep heals its owner's unit standing on it by 10% of max HP;\n485\t  3. map rules run (the Sanctum's Hands and Dials, §6.10; the hub's season advance, §11);\n486\t  4. the win checks run (§5.10).\n487\t- Each new bell tolls a bell sound and the clock face's hand moves.\n488\t\n489\t### 5.4 A unit's turn\n490\t- **Move:** up to MOV, paying terrain costs (§5.7). A unit can't enter or pass enemies, can pass allies, and can't end\n491\t  on an occupied hex. Before acting, a move can be undone with Back.\n492\t- **Then one action, or one action with no move:**\n493\t\n494\t| Action | Rule |\n495\t|---|---|\n496\t| Attack | the unit's basic attack (range and power from its spec); allowed after moving |\n497\t| Special | a skill of kind `special`; after moving only if it is *mobile*; some (Charge, Dive) require moving at least 2 hexes this turn |\n498\t| Spell | a skill of kind `spell`; **only if the unit has not moved this turn** |\n499\t| Item | knights only: a consumable from the realm inventory, on itself or an adjacent ally |\n500\t| Guard | +30% DEF and +10 evasion until its next turn; allowed after moving |\n501\t| Retreat | knights only: the troop leaves the field at once (capture rolls, §5.9). A ruler's retreat loses the battle |\n502\t| Wait | end the unit's turn |\n503\t\n504\t- MP: skills cost MP. Each unit regains 2 MP at its troop's turn start.\n505\t\n506\t### 5.5 Stats\n507\t- HP, MP, ATK, DEF, INT (magic power and magic defense), AGI (evasion, hit, crit, turn order) and MOV.\n508\t- Tags: element (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter or Hour), size (S, M, L), and flags: flier (ignores terrain cost and may\n509\t  cross blocked hexes but not end on ramparts), swimmer (water costs 1, deep water is walkable), floater (swamp and\n510\t  shallows cost 1).\n511\t- Knights also have Bond and Ward radius (§6.6).\n512\t- Levels run from 1 to 40, and 100 EXP gives a level, applied at once with a popup.\n513\t\n514\t### 5.6 Formulas (every constant is in `G.tune`, Appendix A)\n515\t- **Ward:** a monster outside its own knight's Ward (hex distance > radius) has ATK, DEF and INT × (1 − `wardPenalty`\n516\t  0.20).\n517\t- **Hit chance (physical):** `clamp(baseHit 85 + (A.AGI − D.AGI) + sizeHit[A.size][D.size] + flank − terrainEvade(D) −\n518\t  5 × max(0, dist − 2) − weather − (D guarding ? 10 : 0), 15, 99)`.\n519\t  - `sizeHit` (attacker row, target column S / M / L): S: 0 / 0 / +10; M: −10 / 0 / +10; L: −30 / −10 / 0 (the L row\n520\t    is `tune.largeVsSmall`).\n521\t  - `flank` = +5 for each other unit of A's side adjacent to D, at most +15.\n522\t- **Physical damage:** `max(1, round((A.ATK × P − D.DEF × defFactor 0.5) × dmgScale × elem × tide × terrainDef × guard ×\n523\t  surround × crit × var))`.\n524\t  - P is the attack's power (a basic attack is 1.0).\n525\t  - `elem` is 1.30 (`elemStrong`) when A's element opposes D's (Spring ↔ Autumn, Summer ↔ Winter), 0.80 (`elemSame`)\n526\t    when they match, and 1.0 otherwise. Hour is 1.0 both ways, except anti-Hour skills (§6.7).\n527\t  - `tide` = attacker factor × target factor, from §5.11.\n528\t  - `terrainDef` = 1 − D's terrain DEF bonus. `guard` = 0.7 if D guards.\n529\t  - `surround` = 1 + 0.10 × (A's allies adjacent to D, at most 3).\n530\t  - `crit` = 1.5 with chance `critBase` 3% + A.AGI / 4 % (at most 30%).\n531\t  - `var` is uniform between 0.9 and 1.1.\n532\t- **Magic damage (always hits):** `max(1, round((P + A.INT − D.INT × 0.5) × magicScale × elem × tide × var))`, where P\n533\t  is the spell's power (14, 22 or 34 for bolts, storms and tempests). Areas hit everyone in the shape, friends included.\n534\t- **Breath, cone and line specials** use the physical formula, always hit, and apply the element.\n535\t- **Healing:** `round((P + A.INT × 0.8) × healScale)`.\n536\t- **Status chance:** `clamp(base + A.INT − D.INT, 10, 90) × statusScale`. Bosses halve it; the Warding Charm makes its\n537\t  wearer immune to Sleep and Stop.\n538\t- **EXP:**\n539\t  - per damaging hit: `clamp(8 + 2 × (D.level − A.level), 2, 30) × expScale`;\n540\t  - a KO: +20 (a knight +40, a ruler +60);\n541\t  - a heal or buff: +8;\n542\t  - at the end: +10 for each survivor of the winning side, +4 for the losing side.\n543\t- **Level-up growth:** for each stat, `floor(g)` plus 1 more if a seeded roll falls under `g − floor(g)`.\n544\t\n545\t### 5.7 Terrain\n546\t\n547\t| Code | Terrain | Move cost | DEF | Evade | Season transform and notes |\n548\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n549\t| `.` | plain | 1 | 0 | 0 | Winter → snow |\n550\t| `,` | road | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n551\t| `f` | forest | 2 (L: 3; fliers 1) | +20% | +10 | Summer: burns under Summer area spells; Autumn: +10% DEF only (leaf-fall) |\n552\t| `h` | hill | 2 (fliers 1) | +10% | +5 | ranged attacks from a hill get +1 range; melee from a hill +10% damage |\n553\t| `m` | mountain | blocked (fliers 1) | +20% (a perched flier) | +10 | — |\n554\t| `~` | shallows | 2 (swimmers and fliers 1) | −10% | −10 | Spring on flood maps → deep water; Summer: cost 1; Winter → ice |\n555\t| `w` | deep water | blocked (swimmers and fliers 1) | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice |\n556\t| `L` | lake | as deep water | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice (a frozen lake opens the map) |\n557\t| `s` | swamp | 3 (fliers and floaters 1) | −10% | −10 | Summer → plain (dried); Winter: cost 2 |\n558\t| `F` | field | 1 | 0 | 0 | Summer: tall wheat, +10 evade; Autumn: stubble; Winter → snow |\n559\t| `r` | ruins | 1 | +10% | +5 | — |\n560\t| `#` | rampart, gear or building | blocked (fliers may cross but not end there) | — | — | drawn as a raised hex block (§7.2) |\n561\t| `g` | courtyard or gate | 1 | +10% | 0 | — |\n562\t| `b` | bridge | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n563\t| `K` | Keep | 1 | +25% for its owner | 0 | owner heals 10% per bell on it; the attacker's seize objective |\n564\t| `D` | season dial | 1 | 0 | 0 | the Sanctum only (§6.10) |\n565\t| — | snow | 2 for non-Winter walkers, 1 for Winter units and fliers | 0 | 0 | from plain or field in Winter |\n566\t| — | ice | 1 | 0 | −10 | from water in Winter; non-Winter units on ice −10 hit |\n567\t| — | burning forest | 2 | 0 | 0 | lasts 2 bells; a unit starting its turn there takes 10% max HP; then it becomes ash |\n568\t| — | ash | 1 | 0 | 0 | after burning |\n569\t\n570\t### 5.8 Effects (statuses, buffs and debuffs)\n571\t\n572\t| Effect | Kind | Rule | Lasts |\n573\t|---|---|---|---|\n574\t| Poison | status | −8% max HP at its troop's turn start | 3 bells |\n575\t| Burn | status | −5% max HP at turn start, DEF −10% | 2 bells |\n576\t| Chill | status | MOV −1, AGI −20% | 2 bells |\n577\t| Sleep | status | skips its turns; wakes when damaged | 2 bells |\n578\t| Stop | status | skips its next turn, then is immune to Stop for 1 bell | 1 turn |\n579\t| Valor | buff | ATK +20% | 2 bells |\n580\t| Haste | buff | MOV +1, AGI +20% | 2 bells |\n581\t| Warded | buff | DEF +20%, and magic damage taken −20% | 2 bells |\n582\t| Guarded | buff | the Guard action (§5.4) | until its next turn |\n583\t| Weakened | debuff | ATK −15% | 2 bells |\n584\t| Exposed | debuff | DEF −20% | 2 bells |\n585\t\n586\tA unit holds one copy of each effect; reapplying refreshes the duration. Remedy and Purify clear statuses and debuffs.\n587\t\n588\t### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n589\t- When a knight drops to 0 HP or retreats, its troop leaves the field. Each of its monsters still standing rolls for\n590\t  capture if it is adjacent to an enemy knight or inside an enemy knight's Ward:\n591\t  - chance = `captureBase` 25% + 25% if it was outside its own knight's Ward + 15% if below 30% HP, at most 75%;\n592\t  - bosses and Hour elites (Pendulum Wyrm forms) never roll;\n593\t  - a captured monster is taken by the nearest enemy knight (shown with a chain of light). After the battle it joins\n594\t    the winner's reserve at the contested castle if its captor's side won, or the reserve of the captor's home castle\n595\t    if it lost;\n596\t  - every other monster retreats with its knight.\n597\t- If a ruler falls or retreats, every knight on its side retreats at once and the side loses.\n598\t- Monsters at 0 HP die and are gone for good (the Phoenix's Rebirth is the exception, §6.8). Knights at 0 HP are wounded\n599\t  for the next season.\n600\t\n601\t### 5.10 Winning\n602\t- A side loses the moment it has no knights on the field.\n603\t- At the end of the last bell, the attacker wins if one of its knights stands on a Keep hex; otherwise the defender wins\n604\t  and the attackers go home.\n605\t- The Clockwork Sanctum and the hub skirmish have their own rules (§6.10, §11).\n606\t\n607\t### 5.11 Seasons in battle (the Forseasons rules)\n608\t- **Seasonal Tide:** units whose element is the battle's season deal +15% (`tideBonus`) and take 10% less damage. Units\n609\t  of the opposed element deal −15%. Hour units ignore the Tide. Winter of Year 1 is the Long Winter: the Winter Tide is\n610\t  +30%.\n611\t- **Terrain transforms** apply when the battle is built (and at every bell in the hub skirmish): see the season column\n612\t  of §5.7. A map flagged `flood` turns its shallows to deep water in Spring, so bridges become the choke points.\n613\t- **Weather:** Spring rain gives −5 hit to ranged attacks. Summer is clear: Summer area spells set forests burning.\n614\t  Autumn gales give fliers −1 MOV. Winter's cold gives non-Winter units −5 hit.\n615\t- The HUD's season badge says all this in one line, and units affected show ▲ (Tide) or ▼ (against) on their cards.\n616\t\n617\t### 5.12 Forecast\n618\t`sim.forecast(unit, action, target, fromHex)` returns `{ hit, dmg: [min, max], crit, ko, status: [name, chance],\n619\telem: 'strong' | 'weak' | null, tide, captureRisk }` for each unit the action touches. The HUD shows it before every\n620\tconfirm (§8.5.12).\n621\t\n622\t### 5.13 Battle AI (`21-ai-battle.js`)\n623\t- **Per unit, in troop order:** first units that can cast or shoot without moving, then monsters nearest the enemy, and\n624\t  the knight last, so that its Ward covers the troop.\n625\t- For every reachable hex `h` (`grid.reach`, enemies blocked, allies passable) and every legal action and target from\n626\t  `h` (spells only from the start hex), score:\n627\t  - `+ Σ expected damage to foes × (1 + 0.5 × knight + 1.0 × ruler)`;\n628\t  - `+ expected KO bonus` (30, 70 for a knight, 110 for a ruler);\n629\t  - `− 1.5 × expected damage to friends`;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"dd35d116-2537-4467-bbfc-e5da16231722","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:49:54.110Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Who:** any knight who is not a ruler, not wounded and has not moved this Muster. It leaves with its troop for the\n  site's duration (1 or 2 seasons). At most 2 knights per realm may be away at once.\n- **The outcome is rolled at departure** (seeded) and revealed in a vignette when the knight returns. Base weights:\n\n| Outcome | Weight | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Treasure | 30 | an item from the site's pool |\n| Beast | 20 | a monster from the site's pool joins the troop (or the castle reserve), at level = knight level − 2 |\n| Wanderer | 10 (0 if none is free) | a free knight from the site's region joins (§6.5.6) |\n| Mana spring | 15 | +40 to +80 mana |\n| Training | 15 | +60 EXP for the knight, +40 for each monster in its troop |\n| Mishap | 10 | the knight returns wounded (out 1 season); 30% chance its weakest monster is lost |\n\n- **Modifiers:** Cleric line +10 Treasure; Beast line +15 Beast; Ranger line +10 Wanderer; knight level 10 or more:\n  Mishap −5; the Lucky Horseshoe multiplies the four good outcomes by 1.15; a site's focus adds +10 to its outcome (§6.11).\n  Story sites override the table (§6.12).\n\n### 4.10 Equip and items\n- Items sit in one inventory per realm. A knight has three slots: weapon, armor and accessory.\n- Each class line allows certain weapon kinds: Warrior (sword, spear, axe), Ranger (bow), Mage (staff, tome), Cleric\n  (staff, mace), Beast (whip, spear); rulers per class (§6.6).\n- Consumables can be used during Muster on any unit at the same castle. They can also be used in battle by knights\n  (the Item action, §5.4), from the realm inventory.\n\n### 4.11 Promotions and class changes (Muster only, with an animation and a jingle)\n- **Monsters:** tier 2 at level 12, or with the matching Season Seed from level 6; tier 3 at level 22, or with a Seed\n  from level 16. Hour monsters promote by level only. The level stays, the new form's base stats apply, and the bond\n  cost does not change.\n- **Knights:** tier 2 at level 10 (free); tier 3 at level 20 plus a Writ of Knighthood. At the change every stat is\n  multiplied by 1.10 (§6.6).\n\n### 4.12 Declaring a march\n- Pick an enemy or neutral castle adjacent to at least one of yours, then up to 3 knights (each with its troop) from your\n  castles adjacent to the target.\n- Wounded, questing or Stilled knights can't march, and each knight marches at most once a season.\n- Several attacks per season are allowed, one per target.\n- A castle you leave with no knights is open: an enemy attack on it takes it without a battle.\n- Arrows on the map show every declaration (the AI's appear at resolution).\n\n### 4.13 Resolution\n1. Sort every declared attack by the attacker's highest knight level (descending), then by attacking power, then by a\n   seeded tie-break.\n2. For each attack in turn:\n   - If the target already belongs to the attacker, or every attacking troop is gone, skip it.\n   - If the target holds no knights, it changes hands (\"The gates stand open\").\n   - Otherwise there is a battle. If a human commands either side, ask **Command** (fight it) or **Delegate**\n     (auto-resolve, §5.14); otherwise auto-resolve.\n3. Apply the aftermath (§4.14) after each battle, before the next one. Units keep their damage until the next Tidings,\n   so a castle attacked twice in one season fights the second battle hurt.\n\n### 4.14 Aftermath\n- **If the attacker wins:** the castle changes owner and the attacking troops occupy it.\n  - Surviving or retreated defending knights fall back to the nearest castle of their realm, by roads. If that castle\n    is not adjacent, they still go there. If the realm has no castle, it is eliminated.\n  - Unbound monsters in the castle's reserve join the new owner's reserve.\n  - The first time a castle is taken, its treasury item goes to the winner.\n  - A brigand castle taken by a human triggers `brigands_no_more` (§6.12).\n- **If the defender wins:** the attacking troops go home to the castles they came from.\n- **Losses:** knights at 0 HP are wounded (they miss the next season: no move, march or quest, but they can be\n  organized). Monsters at 0 HP are dead. Captures follow §5.9. A ruler at 0 HP or retreating loses the battle for its\n  side.\n- **Elimination:** a realm with no castles is out. Its knights become free and join the wanderer pools of their old\n  regions; its ruler goes into exile. If it was the player's only realm, the game is lost (in hot-seat, that human\n  watches until the game ends).\n\n### 4.15 Campaign AI (`23-ai-campaign.js`, deterministic per seed)\n- **Power:** `power(unit) = (HP + 4 × (ATK + DEF + INT) + 2 × AGI) × (1 + 0.05 × (level − 1))`, ×1.2 for knights. A\n  troop's power is the sum over its units. `defense(c)` = the power of the troops at c × 1.25 (the Keep).\n- **Threat:** `threat(c)` = Σ over adjacent castles of other season-realms (and of the Dominion once it is active) of\n  their marchable power × that realm's aggression (×1.2 in its own season). `need(c) = threat(c) − defense(c)`.\n- **Muster, in order:**\n  1. **Summon** while mana > 1.5 × upkeep + 40. Pick the castle with the highest need. Score each option by power per\n     mana × 1.2 if its element opposes the strongest neighbouring realm's element, × 1.1 if its element is next\n     season's. Bind the monster to a knight there with free Bond, or keep it in reserve.\n  2. **Bind** reserve monsters to knights with free Bond, strongest first.\n  3. **Move** up to 3 troops, each from the castle with the most surplus to an adjacent castle with the highest need.\n     Never leave a border castle (one adjacent to a foe) without a knight.\n  4. **Quest** with knights at interior castles that have no need (at most 2 away), at the site with the best expected\n     value.\n  5. **Equip** the best item per slot (ATK for warriors, rangers and tamers; INT for mages and clerics; armor by DEF;\n     accessories by Bond, then Spurs, then Ward). **Promote** and class-change whenever eligible.\n- **March:**\n  - For each adjacent foreign castle, the attackers are troops that are not needed at home. A troop is needed if taking\n    it leaves `need(c) > 0.4 × threat(c)` or leaves a border castle empty.\n  - `ratio = Σ top-3 attacker power / defense(target)` (an empty castle is ∞). Attack if `ratio ≥ threshold /\n    aggression`, where threshold is 1.6 / 1.3 / 1.1 on Easy / Normal / Hard.\n  - Target value: Meridian ×1.5 (if the realm holds an adjacent satellite), capitals ×1.3, brigand castles ×1.2 in Year\n    1; then the highest ratio. Each troop marches once.\n- **Personalities:**\n\n| Realm | Aggression | Quirk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Solmark | 1.15 | ×1.3 in Summer; prefers the weakest neighbour |\n| Hoarfast | rolled each season between 0.9 and 1.4 (\"the Duke's moods\") | ×1.3 in Winter |\n| Amberlyn | 0.85 | sends up to 3 questers; keeps one extra troop at its capital |\n| Verdance | 1.0 | takes brigand castles first |\n| Hourless Dominion | 0 in Year 1, 0.8 in Year 2, 1.1 from Year 3 | never leaves Meridian with fewer than 2 troops; summons only Hour monsters |\n| Brigands | 0 | never march or summon; full HP at each Tidings |\n\n### 4.16 Stillness\nFrom Autumn of Year 3, each Tidings the Gray Knight stills one castle (seeded) that borders Dominion territory, other\nthan Meridian. For that season it yields no mana, and its troops can't move, march or quest (they defend normally). It\nis drawn in grey with a stopped-clock icon. The first time, the `stillness` event plays; after that a toast announces it.\n\n### 4.17 Winning and losing\n- **Win:** defeat the Gray Knight in the Clockwork Sanctum. That battle becomes available the moment your realm takes\n  Meridian (§6.12, `meridian_falls`). If you lose it, your troops fall back into Meridian, and you can attack the\n  Sanctum again from Meridian in a later March (the Sanctum shows as a special target beside Meridian).\n- **Lose:**\n  - your realm loses its last castle;\n  - the candle burns out;\n  - or a rival realm holds Meridian and wins its Sanctum battle. When an AI realm takes Meridian, it fights the Sanctum,\n    auto-resolved, at the next Tidings. If it wins, it \"sets the Wheel\" to its season and you lose (a rival's bad\n    ending). If it loses, Meridian returns to the Dominion with a fresh garrison (2 troops, level 14).\n- **Hot-seat:** the first human to win wins for everyone; the others see their own epilogue card.\n\n### 4.18 Difficulty (chosen for each new campaign)\n\n| | Easy | Normal | Hard |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AI mana income | ×0.8 | ×1.0 | ×1.25 |\n| AI march threshold | 1.6 | 1.3 | 1.1 |\n| Candle seasons | 16 | 12 | 10 |\n| Enemy battle AI | picks from its top 3, weighted | the best plan | the best plan, plus focus fire |\n| Player EXP | ×1.25 | ×1.0 | ×1.0 |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Battle rules (`BattleSim`)\n\n### 5.1 The field\n- Pointy-top hexes in offset rows (odd rows shifted right): `new E.Grid(w, h, { hex: 'pointy', walkable, cost })`.\n- A hex is `T = 28` world units across the flats; `grid.center(c, 28)` gives its centre.\n- Maps run from 13 × 9 to 17 × 13 hexes, with one unit per hex.\n- The field is flat (z = 0). Height comes from terrain types and props, as in the source's flat hex maps. Raised blocks\n  (ramparts, gears, cliffs) are impassable shapes (§7.2).\n\n### 5.2 Sides and deployment\n- Two sides, attacker and defender, each with up to 3 troops. A troop is one knight and up to 6 monsters.\n- Troop anchors are hexes `1 2 3` (attacker) and `7 8 9` (defender). The defender's first troop takes the anchor next to\n  the Keep. Skirmish and hub maps use seat anchors `1 2 3 4`.\n- The knight stands on the anchor, and its monsters fill the free hexes nearest it according to its formation:\n  - **Vanguard:** hexes 1–2 steps toward the enemy's side first.\n  - **Shield:** the ring around the knight first.\n  - **Column:** a line behind the knight, away from the enemy.\n- Units face the enemy side.\n\n### 5.3 Bells and turn order\n- A battle lasts up to `tune.bells` (12) bells.\n- Each bell, troops act in order of their knight's AGI (descending; ties go to the defender, then the lower troop id).\n- In a troop's turn, each of its units acts once, in any order its controller likes. The troop ends when all have acted\n  or its controller ends it (the rest Wait). A troop whose knight has fallen is gone.\n- **At the end of each bell:**\n  1. effects tick (§5.8);\n  2. the Keep heals its owner's unit standing on it by 10% of max HP;\n  3. map rules run (the Sanctum's Hands and Dials, §6.10; the hub's season advance, §11);\n  4. the win checks run (§5.10).\n- Each new bell tolls a bell sound and the clock face's hand moves.\n\n### 5.4 A unit's turn\n- **Move:** up to MOV, paying terrain costs (§5.7). A unit can't enter or pass enemies, can pass allies, and can't end\n  on an occupied hex. Before acting, a move can be undone with Back.\n- **Then one action, or one action with no move:**\n\n| Action | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Attack | the unit's basic attack (range and power from its spec); allowed after moving |\n| Special | a skill of kind `special`; after moving only if it is *mobile*; some (Charge, Dive) require moving at least 2 hexes this turn |\n| Spell | a skill of kind `spell`; **only if the unit has not moved this turn** |\n| Item | knights only: a consumable from the realm inventory, on itself or an adjacent ally |\n| Guard | +30% DEF and +10 evasion until its next turn; allowed after moving |\n| Retreat | knights only: the troop leaves the field at once (capture rolls, §5.9). A ruler's retreat loses the battle |\n| Wait | end the unit's turn |\n\n- MP: skills cost MP. Each unit regains 2 MP at its troop's turn start.\n\n### 5.5 Stats\n- HP, MP, ATK, DEF, INT (magic power and magic defense), AGI (evasion, hit, crit, turn order) and MOV.\n- Tags: element (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter or Hour), size (S, M, L), and flags: flier (ignores terrain cost and may\n  cross blocked hexes but not end on ramparts), swimmer (water costs 1, deep water is walkable), floater (swamp and\n  shallows cost 1).\n- Knights also have Bond and Ward radius (§6.6).\n- Levels run from 1 to 40, and 100 EXP gives a level, applied at once with a popup.\n\n### 5.6 Formulas (every constant is in `G.tune`, Appendix A)\n- **Ward:** a monster outside its own knight's Ward (hex distance > radius) has ATK, DEF and INT × (1 − `wardPenalty`\n  0.20).\n- **Hit chance (physical):** `clamp(baseHit 85 + (A.AGI − D.AGI) + sizeHit[A.size][D.size] + flank − terrainEvade(D) −\n  5 × max(0, dist − 2) − weather − (D guarding ? 10 : 0), 15, 99)`.\n  - `sizeHit` (attacker row, target column S / M / L): S: 0 / 0 / +10; M: −10 / 0 / +10; L: −30 / −10 / 0 (the L row\n    is `tune.largeVsSmall`).\n  - `flank` = +5 for each other unit of A's side adjacent to D, at most +15.\n- **Physical damage:** `max(1, round((A.ATK × P − D.DEF × defFactor 0.5) × dmgScale × elem × tide × terrainDef × guard ×\n  surround × crit × var))`.\n  - P is the attack's power (a basic attack is 1.0).\n  - `elem` is 1.30 (`elemStrong`) when A's element opposes D's (Spring ↔ Autumn, Summer ↔ Winter), 0.80 (`elemSame`)\n    when they match, and 1.0 otherwise. Hour is 1.0 both ways, except anti-Hour skills (§6.7).\n  - `tide` = attacker factor × target factor, from §5.11.\n  - `terrainDef` = 1 − D's terrain DEF bonus. `guard` = 0.7 if D guards.\n  - `surround` = 1 + 0.10 × (A's allies adjacent to D, at most 3).\n  - `crit` = 1.5 with chance `critBase` 3% + A.AGI / 4 % (at most 30%).\n  - `var` is uniform between 0.9 and 1.1.\n- **Magic damage (always hits):** `max(1, round((P + A.INT − D.INT × 0.5) × magicScale × elem × tide × var))`, where P\n  is the spell's power (14, 22 or 34 for bolts, storms and tempests). Areas hit everyone in the shape, friends included.\n- **Breath, cone and line specials** use the physical formula, always hit, and apply the element.\n- **Healing:** `round((P + A.INT × 0.8) × healScale)`.\n- **Status chance:** `clamp(base + A.INT − D.INT, 10, 90) × statusScale`. Bosses halve it; the Warding Charm makes its\n  wearer immune to Sleep and Stop.\n- **EXP:**\n  - per damaging hit: `clamp(8 + 2 × (D.level − A.level), 2, 30) × expScale`;\n  - a KO: +20 (a knight +40, a ruler +60);\n  - a heal or buff: +8;\n  - at the end: +10 for each survivor of the winning side, +4 for the losing side.\n- **Level-up growth:** for each stat, `floor(g)` plus 1 more if a seeded roll falls under `g − floor(g)`.\n\n### 5.7 Terrain\n\n| Code | Terrain | Move cost | DEF | Evade | Season transform and notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `.` | plain | 1 | 0 | 0 | Winter → snow |\n| `,` | road | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n| `f` | forest | 2 (L: 3; fliers 1) | +20% | +10 | Summer: burns under Summer area spells; Autumn: +10% DEF only (leaf-fall) |\n| `h` | hill | 2 (fliers 1) | +10% | +5 | ranged attacks from a hill get +1 range; melee from a hill +10% damage |\n| `m` | mountain | blocked (fliers 1) | +20% (a perched flier) | +10 | — |\n| `~` | shallows | 2 (swimmers and fliers 1) | −10% | −10 | Spring on flood maps → deep water; Summer: cost 1; Winter → ice |\n| `w` | deep water | blocked (swimmers and fliers 1) | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice |\n| `L` | lake | as deep water | 0 | 0 | Winter → ice (a frozen lake opens the map) |\n| `s` | swamp | 3 (fliers and floaters 1) | −10% | −10 | Summer → plain (dried); Winter: cost 2 |\n| `F` | field | 1 | 0 | 0 | Summer: tall wheat, +10 evade; Autumn: stubble; Winter → snow |\n| `r` | ruins | 1 | +10% | +5 | — |\n| `#` | rampart, gear or building | blocked (fliers may cross but not end there) | — | — | drawn as a raised hex block (§7.2) |\n| `g` | courtyard or gate | 1 | +10% | 0 | — |\n| `b` | bridge | 1 | 0 | 0 | — |\n| `K` | Keep | 1 | +25% for its owner | 0 | owner heals 10% per bell on it; the attacker's seize objective |\n| `D` | season dial | 1 | 0 | 0 | the Sanctum only (§6.10) |\n| — | snow | 2 for non-Winter walkers, 1 for Winter units and fliers | 0 | 0 | from plain or field in Winter |\n| — | ice | 1 | 0 | −10 | from water in Winter; non-Winter units on ice −10 hit |\n| — | burning forest | 2 | 0 | 0 | lasts 2 bells; a unit starting its turn there takes 10% max HP; then it becomes ash |\n| — | ash | 1 | 0 | 0 | after burning |\n\n### 5.8 Effects (statuses, buffs and debuffs)\n\n| Effect | Kind | Rule | Lasts |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Poison | status | −8% max HP at its troop's turn start | 3 bells |\n| Burn | status | −5% max HP at turn start, DEF −10% | 2 bells |\n| Chill | status | MOV −1, AGI −20% | 2 bells |\n| Sleep | status | skips its turns; wakes when damaged | 2 bells |\n| Stop | status | skips its next turn, then is immune to Stop for 1 bell | 1 turn |\n| Valor | buff | ATK +20% | 2 bells |\n| Haste | buff | MOV +1, AGI +20% | 2 bells |\n| Warded | buff | DEF +20%, and magic damage taken −20% | 2 bells |\n| Guarded | buff | the Guard action (§5.4) | until its next turn |\n| Weakened | debuff | ATK −15% | 2 bells |\n| Exposed | debuff | DEF −20% | 2 bells |\n\nA unit holds one copy of each effect; reapplying refreshes the duration. Remedy and Purify clear statuses and debuffs.\n\n### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n- When a knight drops to 0 HP or retreats, its troop leaves the field. Each of its monsters still standing rolls for\n  capture if it is adjacent to an enemy knight or inside an enemy knight's Ward:\n  - chance = `captureBase` 25% + 25% if it was outside its own knight's Ward + 15% if below 30% HP, at most 75%;\n  - bosses and Hour elites (Pendulum Wyrm forms) never roll;\n  - a captured monster is taken by the nearest enemy knight (shown with a chain of light). After the battle it joins\n    the winner's reserve at the contested castle if its captor's side won, or the reserve of the captor's home castle\n    if it lost;\n  - every other monster retreats with its knight.\n- If a ruler falls or retreats, every knight on its side retreats at once and the side loses.\n- Monsters at 0 HP die and are gone for good (the Phoenix's Rebirth is the exception, §6.8). Knights at 0 HP are wounded\n  for the next season.\n\n### 5.10 Winning\n- A side loses the moment it has no knights on the field.\n- At the end of the last bell, the attacker wins if one of its knights stands on a Keep hex; otherwise the defender wins\n  and the attackers go home.\n- The Clockwork Sanctum and the hub skirmish have their own rules (§6.10, §11).\n\n### 5.11 Seasons in battle (the Forseasons rules)\n- **Seasonal Tide:** units whose element is the battle's season deal +15% (`tideBonus`) and take 10% less damage. Units\n  of the opposed element deal −15%. Hour units ignore the Tide. Winter of Year 1 is the Long Winter: the Winter Tide is\n  +30%.\n- **Terrain transforms** apply when the battle is built (and at every bell in the hub skirmish): see the season column\n  of §5.7. A map flagged `flood` turns its shallows to deep water in Spring, so bridges become the choke points.\n- **Weather:** Spring rain gives −5 hit to ranged attacks. Summer is clear: Summer area spells set forests burning.\n  Autumn gales give fliers −1 MOV. Winter's cold gives non-Winter units −5 hit.\n- The HUD's season badge says all this in one line, and units affected show ▲ (Tide) or ▼ (against) on their cards.\n\n### 5.12 Forecast\n`sim.forecast(unit, action, target, fromHex)` returns `{ hit, dmg: [min, max], crit, ko, status: [name, chance],\nelem: 'strong' | 'weak' | null, tide, captureRisk }` for each unit the action touches. The HUD shows it before every\nconfirm (§8.5.12).\n\n### 5.13 Battle AI (`21-ai-battle.js`)\n- **Per unit, in troop order:** first units that can cast or shoot without moving, then monsters nearest the enemy, and\n  the knight last, so that its Ward covers the troop.\n- For every reachable hex `h` (`grid.reach`, enemies blocked, allies passable) and every legal action and target from\n  `h` (spells only from the start hex), score:\n  - `+ Σ expected damage to foes × (1 + 0.5 × knight + 1.0 × ruler)`;\n  - `+ expected KO bonus` (30, 70 for a knight, 110 for a ruler);\n  - `− 1.5 × expected damage to friends`;","numLines":300,"startLine":330,"totalLines":2404}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DU8M8Jv6bBpyFUeLr6MouS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
