{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cqeo7YbcKyUGTxz75CUXDy","type":"tool_result","content":"629\t  - `− 1.5 × expected damage to friends`;\n630\t  - `+ 1.2 × healing × (knight ? 2 : 1)`;\n631\t  - `− danger(h) × (knight ? 1.5 : 0.6) × (HP < 40% ? 2 : 1)`, where `danger(h)` is the expected damage foes could deal\n632\t    at `h` next bell;\n633\t  - `− 12` if a monster ends outside its Ward;\n634\t  - `+ 10 × terrain DEF`;\n635\t  - objective terms: from bell 8, attackers `− 2 × distance(h, Keep)` and defending knights `− 3 × distance(h, Keep)`;\n636\t  - when no target is in reach: melee `− 1.2 × distance to the nearest foe`; ranged and casters `− 1.5 × |distance −\n637\t    3|`.\n638\t- Take the best score; ties go to the first in a fixed order.\n639\t- A non-ruler knight below 25% HP whose side is losing on power may Retreat. Rulers never retreat (their danger weight is\n640\t  ×3 instead).\n641\t- Easy picks among its top 3 (weights 3 : 2 : 1); Hard adds +15 for targets already damaged this bell.\n642\t- The same state always gives the same plan, so a bot running both sides is a repeatable test.\n643\t\n644\t### 5.14 Delegate (auto-resolve) and speed\n645\t- **Delegate** runs the same `BattleSim` with the AI on both sides to the end, in one synchronous loop with no drawing,\n646\t  and shows a summary card (losses, captures, level-ups).\n647\t- Animation speed comes from the setting (Full, Fast, Minimal). Holding ✕/Enter during AI turns plays at 4×.\n648\t\n649\t---\n650\t\n651\t## 6. Content\n652\t\n653\t### 6.1 The world: Forseason\n654\t- **Shape:** a round continent (radius about 470 world units) on a 1024 × 1024 map (64 × 64 tiles), with the sea all\n655\t  around it.\n656\t- **The centre:** the grey Hour plateau with Meridian, the Calendar City, whose great clock tower is visible from\n657\t  everywhere.\n658\t- **The four quarters, one realm each, each in its native season's look:**\n659\t  - north, Hoarfast: snowfields, pine forests, frozen lakes and the Rimewall mountains;\n660\t  - east, Verdance: green meadows, blossoming orchards, rivers and lakes, spring rain;\n661\t  - south, Solmark: golden savanna, red mesas, dunes and palms along the coast;\n662\t  - west, Amberlyn: amber farmland, oak woods, pumpkin fields, misty bogs and watermills.\n663\t- **The cross-quarter marches** (NE Thaw, SE Beltane, SW Lammas, NW Hallow) blend their two neighbours. Brigand free\n664\t  companies hold them.\n665\t- **The current season tints everything:** a dusting of snow in Winter, blossoms in Spring, gold in Summer, falling\n666\t  leaves in Autumn.\n667\t\n668\t### 6.2 Castles (positions in world units on the 1024 × 1024 map)\n669\t\n670\t| id | Name | Region | Tier | Start owner | Mana | Battle map | Summon circle (tier-1 species; a season in brackets means only then) | Quest site | Treasury | Pos |\n671\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n672\t| meridian | Meridian, the Calendar City | hour | capital | Dominion | 60 | meridian_clockyard | minute, clockwork, gearhound, stillwraith, pendulumwyrm | The Sleeping Court | Hourglass Rod | 512,512 |\n673\t| midnight | Midnight Keep | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, stillwraith, gearhound | The Bell That Doesn't Ring | Writ of Knighthood | 512,392 |\n674\t| dawnwatch | Dawnwatch | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, clockwork, gearhound | The Sunrise Stair | Swift Spurs | 632,512 |\n675\t| noonspire | Noonspire | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | crossroads | clockwork, gearhound, minute | The Shadowless Square | Signet of Command | 512,632 |\n676\t| vesperhall | Vesper Hall | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | ruined_abbey | stillwraith, minute, clockwork | The Evensong Crypt | Writ of Knighthood | 392,512 |\n677\t| rimeholt | Rimeholt | winter | capital | Hoarfast | 40 | capital_citadel | snowkit, frostwolf, icegolem, yeti, frostwyrm (Winter) | The Lake of Silent Bells | Frostplate | 512,92 |\n678\t| wolfsgate | Wolfsgate | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | mountain_pass | frostwolf, snowkit, yeti | The Howling Scar | Winter Shard | 352,235 |\n679\t| frostmere | Frostmere | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | lakeside | snowkit, icegolem, frostwolf | Nimue's Mere | Warding Charm | 672,235 |\n680\t| kestrel | Kestrel Spire | winter | inner | Hoarfast | 25 | forest_hold | frostwolf, yeti, snowkit | The Kestrel Eyrie | Yew Longbow | 512,277 |\n681\t| avalorn | Avalorn | spring | capital | Verdance | 40 | capital_citadel | sproutling, pixie, unicorn, treant, rillserpent (Spring) | The Queen's Orchard | Robe of Seasons | 932,512 |\n682\t| thornwick | Thornwick | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | forest_hold | sproutling, treant, pixie | The Briar Maze | Thornmail | 789,352 |\n683\t| rainmere | Rainmere | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | river_ford | rillserpent, sproutling, pixie | The Weeping Weir | Spring Seed | 789,672 |\n684\t| primrose | Primrose Ford | spring | inner | Verdance | 25 | lakeside | unicorn, pixie, sproutling | The Unicorn Glade | Tome of Thaw | 747,512 |\n685\t| brazenhold | Brazenhold | summer | capital | Solmark | 40 | capital_citadel | salamander, cinderhound, sunbird, sunmane, wyvern (Summer) | The Furnace Vaults | Sunforged Blade | 512,932 |\n686\t| goldspur | Goldspur | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | crossroads | salamander, cinderhound, wyvern (Summer) | The Wyvern Roost | Summer Ember | 672,789 |\n687\t| cinderwall | Cinderwall | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | mountain_pass | cinderhound, salamander, sunmane | The Ash Dunes | Mail Hauberk | 352,789 |\n688\t| lionsreach | Lionsreach | summer | inner | Solmark | 25 | hill_fort | sunmane, sunbird, cinderhound | The Lion Steps | Banner Pin | 512,747 |\n689\t| ambergate | Ambergate | autumn | capital | Amberlyn | 40 | capital_citadel | jacklamp, scarecrow, ghoul, tusker, griffin (Autumn) | The Harvest Vault | Lantern Staff | 92,512 |\n690\t| ashbarrow | Ashbarrow | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | ruined_abbey | ghoul, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Barrow Downs | Autumn Acorn | 235,352 |\n691\t| russetmoor | Russetmoor | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | marsh_keep | tusker, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Russet Bog | Lucky Horseshoe | 235,672 |\n692\t| lanternfall | Lanternfall | autumn | inner | Amberlyn | 25 | forest_hold | jacklamp, ghoul, scarecrow | The Lantern Road | Ring of Mending | 277,512 |\n693\t| thawgate | Thawgate | thaw (winter/spring) | cross | Brigands: Hob Mudspur | 30 | river_ford | snowkit, sproutling, slime, bat | The Breaking Ice | Golden Draught | 756,268 |\n694\t| beltane | Beltane Ford | beltane (spring/summer) | cross | Brigands: Mother Gerrow | 30 | marsh_keep | sproutling, salamander, slime, harpy | The Old Mill of Beltane | Amulet of Tides | 756,756 |\n695\t| lammas | Lammas Cross | lammas (summer/autumn) | cross | Brigands: Red Dafydd | 30 | crossroads | salamander, scarecrow, skeleton, ogre | The Lammas Fair | Thorn Whip | 268,756 |\n696\t| hallowmere | Hallowmere | hallow (autumn/winter) | cross | Brigands: the Hollow Abbot | 30 | ruined_abbey | jacklamp, snowkit, skeleton, bat | The Hollow Abbey Crypts | Hawthorn Bow | 268,268 |\n697\t\n698\tA battle map's dressing (tree kinds, palette, props, castle style) follows the castle's region; terrain then follows the\n699\tbattle's season (§5.11). A cross-quarter castle's season bonus applies in both of its seasons.\n700\t\n701\t### 6.3 Roads (36)\n702\t- **Hoarfast:** rimeholt–wolfsgate, rimeholt–frostmere, wolfsgate–kestrel, frostmere–kestrel.\n703\t- **Verdance:** avalorn–thornwick, avalorn–rainmere, thornwick–primrose, rainmere–primrose.\n704\t- **Solmark:** brazenhold–goldspur, brazenhold–cinderwall, goldspur–lionsreach, cinderwall–lionsreach.\n705\t- **Amberlyn:** ambergate–ashbarrow, ambergate–russetmoor, ashbarrow–lanternfall, russetmoor–lanternfall.\n706\t- **Cross-quarters:** thawgate–frostmere, thawgate–thornwick, beltane–rainmere, beltane–goldspur, lammas–cinderwall,\n707\t  lammas–russetmoor, hallowmere–ashbarrow, hallowmere–wolfsgate.\n708\t- **Into the Hourlands:** kestrel–midnight, primrose–dawnwatch, lionsreach–noonspire, lanternfall–vesperhall.\n709\t- **The Hour ring:** midnight–dawnwatch, dawnwatch–noonspire, noonspire–vesperhall, vesperhall–midnight.\n710\t- **To Meridian:** meridian–midnight, meridian–dawnwatch, meridian–noonspire, meridian–vesperhall.\n711\t\n712\tEvery realm has the same shape: a capital at the back, two flank castles that each face a brigand castle, and an inner\n713\tcastle that faces an Hour satellite. That keeps the realms fair. A test checks the graph is connected and symmetric.\n714\t\n715\t### 6.4 Realms\n716\t\n717\t| id | Realm | Season | Colours (main / trim) | Sigil | Banner | Ruler | Capital |\n718\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n719\t| verdance | Kingdom of Verdance | Spring | `#4caf50` / `#f0e6c8` | five-petal blossom | swallowtail | Prince Gareth Greenmantle | Avalorn |\n720\t| solmark | Sun-March of Solmark | Summer | `#e0a020` / `#b02a2a` | rayed sun | square | Queen Morgause the Brazen | Brazenhold |\n721\t| amberlyn | Harvest Throne of Amberlyn | Autumn | `#c86a1e` / `#5a3a2a` | oak leaf | pointed | King Pellam the Quiet | Ambergate |\n722\t| hoarfast | Duchy of Hoarfast | Winter | `#6ab0e8` / `#e8f4ff` | snowflake | triangle | Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten | Rimeholt |\n723\t| dominion | Hourless Dominion | Hour | `#3a3a46` / `#d8c070` | hourglass | long tapered | Lord Chancellor Meliant | Meridian |\n724\t| brigands | Free Companies | — | `#7a6a5a` / `#2a2a2a` | crossed axes | ragged | (four captains) | — |\n725\t\n726\tSides are never told apart by colour alone: every unit also carries its realm's sigil on a pennant over it, and the\n727\toutline colour, the banner shape and the sigil all agree.\n728\t\n729\t### 6.5 Knights\n730\tEach row gives the Humanoid look (§7.5) and the voice profile (§9.3). Each troop lists `species level`. Every realm's\n731\tcapital also starts with two tier-1 level-2 monsters in reserve: Verdance sproutlings, Solmark salamanders, Amberlyn\n732\tjack-o'-lamps and Hoarfast snowkits. Meridian starts with two level-10 minutes.\n733\t\n734\t#### 6.5.1 Verdance (Spring)\n735\t\n736\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n737\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n738\t| gareth | **Prince Gareth Greenmantle** (ruler) | Springwarden | 6 | Spring | Avalorn | unicorn 4, pixie 4, sproutling 4 | earnest, idealistic, quick to forgive; grieving his mother, the late Queen | heroic 1.25, armor, short golden hair, circlet, green cape, sword | bright tenor, quick |\n739\t| lynette | Dame Lynette of Thornwick | Squire | 7 | Spring | Thornwick | treant 4, sproutling 3 | his sworn shield; stern, dry humour, protective | heroic 1.2, armor, dark-red ponytail, band, white-and-green tabard | firm alto |\n740\t| pelleas | Sir Pelleas the Lovelorn | Archer | 5 | Spring | Primrose Ford | pixie 4, rillserpent 3 | a poet-archer, overdramatic and brave | heroic 1.15, tunic, long chestnut hair, cap | lilting, high |\n741\t| amris | Brother Amris | Acolyte | 6 | Winter | Avalorn | snowkit 3, sproutling 3 | an old monk from the north; gentle, wry | heroic 1.15, hunch .2, grey robe, bald, staff | slow, low |\n742\t| wren | Wren Ashfeather | Tamer | 5 | Spring | Rainmere | unicorn 3, pixie 3, sproutling 3 | raised among unicorns; few words | heroic 1.1, leaf-green tunic, ash-white spiky hair, hood | chirpy |\n743\t\n744\t#### 6.5.2 Solmark (Summer)\n745\t\n746\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n747\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n748\t| morgause | **Queen Morgause the Brazen** (ruler) | Sun Sovereign | 7 | Summer | Brazenhold | wyvern 4, cinderhound 4 | magnificent and war-loving, honourable on the field, ruthless at court | heroic 1.3, gold armor, crown, long copper hair, crimson cape, two-handed sword | commanding mezzo |\n749\t| agravain | Sir Agravain Cinderjaw | Squire | 7 | Summer | Cinderwall | cinderhound 4, salamander 3 | a hothead champion who craves glory | bulky 1.25, armor, helmet, red cape | growly baritone |\n750\t| elidure | Captain Elidure of Goldspur | Archer | 6 | Summer | Goldspur | sunbird 3, salamander 3 | disciplined, loyal and secretly kind | heroic 1.2, sand coat, black ponytail, band | clear soprano |\n751\t| hesper | Magus Hesper Vey | Adept | 6 | Hour | Lionsreach | salamander 3, minute 3 | an ambitious court sorcerer who dabbles in Hour magic | heroic 1.2, purple-and-gold robe, pointed hat, long silver hair | silky |\n752\t| brennoc | Old Brennoc | Tamer | 5 | Summer | Brazenhold | sunmane 3, cinderhound 3 | a grizzled, grandfatherly beastkeeper | bulky 1.2, hunch .3, leather coat, bald, whip | gravelly |\n753\t\n754\t#### 6.5.3 Amberlyn (Autumn)\n755\t\n756\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n757\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n758\t| pellam | **King Pellam the Quiet** (ruler) | Harvest King | 8 | Autumn | Ambergate | griffin 4, scarecrow 4 | silent and wise; speaks rarely and briefly; secretly ill | heroic 1.2, hunch .25, amber-and-umber robe, crown, long white hair, staff | soft, low, slow |\n759\t| enid | Lady Enid Russet | Acolyte | 6 | Autumn | Ambergate | jacklamp 3, scarecrow 3 | the king's daughter; gentle, firm, practical | heroic 1.15, cream-and-russet robe, long auburn hair, band | warm |\n760\t| dagonet | Sir Dagonet the Motley | Squire | 5 | Autumn | Russetmoor | tusker 3, jacklamp 3 | a jester-knight who jokes to hide his fear | heroic 1.1, two-colour tunic, pointed hat, sword | bouncy |\n761\t| vesna | Vesna of the Lanterns | Adept | 6 | Summer | Lanternfall | jacklamp 4, ghoul 3 | a lamplighter witch, kind to the dead | heroic 1.15, black-and-orange robe, pointed hat, long black hair | breathy |\n762\t| lamorak | Sir Lamorak Ashbarrow | Squire | 8 | Autumn | Ashbarrow | ghoul 4, scarecrow 3 | a gruff old veteran, loyal to Pellam | bulky 1.2, rusty armor, helmet, brown cape | gruff |\n763\t\n764\t#### 6.5.4 Hoarfast (Winter)\n765\t\n766\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n767\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n768\t| mordrain | **Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten** (ruler) | Rime Duke | 7 | Winter | Rimeholt | frostwyrm 3, snowkit 4 | theatrical, mad and brilliant; speaks in riddles; grief hidden under ice | heroic 1.25, white coat, icicle crown, long white hair, staff, pale-blue cape, faint eyeGlow | high, erratic pitch |\n769\t| ragnell | Dame Ragnell Ice-Eye | Squire | 8 | Winter | Kestrel Spire | frostwolf 4, icegolem 3 | his cold, calculating marshal, the sane one | heroic 1.25, steel armor, helmet, white ponytail, dark-blue cape | flat alto |\n770\t| safir | Sir Safir the Pale | Archer | 6 | Winter | Wolfsgate | frostwolf 3, snowkit 3 | a quiet, melancholic hunter | heroic 1.2, white hood, grey coat | soft |\n771\t| nimue | Nimue of Frostmere | Adept | 7 | Winter | Frostmere | snowkit 4, snowkit 3 | an enigmatic lake witch who makes bargains | heroic 1.15, teal robe, long pale-blue hair | echoing |\n772\t| gorm | Gorm the Bear | Tamer | 5 | Autumn | Rimeholt | yeti 3, tusker 3 | huge and gentle; raised in the western woods | bulky 1.35, brown fur coat, short hair, whip | very low |\n773\t\n774\t#### 6.5.5 The Hourless Dominion (Hour)\n775\t\n776\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n777\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n778\t| meliant | **Lord Chancellor Meliant** (ruler) | Chancellor of Hours | 14 | Meridian | pendulumwyrm 10, clockwork (tier 2: Tick Knight) 12, stillwraith 12 | cold, grieving and absolute; believes he is merciful | heroic 1.25, black-and-brass robe, brass band, short grey hair, brass rod | measured baritone |\n779\t| bertilak | Marshal Bertilak the Hourward | Knight | 12 | Midnight Keep | clockwork (tier 2) 12, gearhound 10, gearhound 9 | courteous, ruthless; loves a duel | bulky 1.3, brass armor, helmet, green-black cape | booming |\n780\t| aurelie | Countess Aurelie of Vespers | Sorcerer | 12 | Vesper Hall | stillwraith 10, minute 10, minute 9 | elegant, bored and cruel | heroic 1.2, violet-and-black robe, long black hair, band | drawling |\n781\t| morholt | Sir Morholt the Unmoving | Knight | 11 | Noonspire | clockwork 10, clockwork 9 | a silent giant | bulky 1.45, black armor, helmet | grunts only |\n782\t| tic | Tic | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | a clockwork twin who finishes Tac's sentences | chibi 1.0, brass armor, cap | squeaky, high |\n783\t| tac | Tac | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | the other twin | the same, colours swapped | squeaky, low |\n784\t| graynight | **The Gray Knight, Sir Nonesuch** | Knight of the Thirteenth Hour | 25 | the Sanctum only | minute (tier 3) 22 ×4, pendulumwyrm (tier 2) 22 | the month that never was: calm, ancient, faintly amused | heroic 1.6, grey armor, helmet, tattered grey cape, white eyeGlow, long sword, clock-hand halo | two detuned low voices |\n785\t\n786\tThe Gray Knight's stats are fixed: HP 900, MP 200, ATK 52, DEF 48, INT 50, AGI 30, MOV 5. His skills are Thirteenth\n787\tStroke, Still, Unmaking and Timeless.\n788\t\n789\t#### 6.5.6 Free knights (joined by event or quest)\n790\t\n791\t| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | How they join | Brings | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n792\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n793\t| lunete | Princess Lunete of Meridian | Hourmaiden | 8 | Hour | the Lunete chain (§6.12) | — | the Keeper's daughter; steady and kind; carries her father's broken watch | heroic 1.15, white-and-brass robe, long gold hair, band | clear, gentle |\n794\t| galeron | Sir Galeron the Wanderer | Knight | 10 | Spring | Wanderer outcome at Winter or Spring sites, from Autumn of Year 1 | frostwolf 8 | an errant knight looking for a cause | heroic 1.25, dented armor, faded green cape | weary tenor |\n795\t| blanchefleur | Blanchefleur the Sellsword | Ranger | 10 | Autumn | Wanderer at Summer or Autumn sites, or the Lammas Fair (pay 150 mana) | sunmane 8 | a mercenary with a code: coin first | heroic 1.2, red-brown coat, short blonde hair | brisk |\n796\t| owain | Owain the Dragonless | Beastlord | 11 | Summer | event `owain`: the first time your realm binds a wyvern or frost wyrm | — | lost his dragon in the Long Winter; will train yours | bulky 1.25, leather coat, short hair | husky |\n797\t| ettard | Sister Ettard | Priest | 10 | Winter | Wanderer at Hallowmere, Lanternfall or Frostmere | snowkit 7 | a sharp-tongued healer | heroic 1.15, white-and-blue robe, hood | crisp |\n798\t\n799\t#### 6.5.7 Brigand captains (Brigand Captain class)\n800\t\n801\t| id | Name | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are |\n802\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n803\t| hob | Hob Mudspur | 5 | Winter | Thawgate | snowkit 4, frostwolf 4, bat 3, slime 3 | swaggering, and a coward at heart |\n804\t| gerrow | Mother Gerrow | 5 | Spring | Beltane Ford | slime 4, harpy 4, sproutling 3, bat 3 | motherly and crafty; hides Lunete at her mill |\n805\t| dafydd | Red Dafydd | 6 | Summer | Lammas Cross | ogre 4, skeleton 4, salamander 3 | boisterous and proud |\n806\t| abbot | The Hollow Abbot | 6 | Autumn | Hallowmere | skeleton 5, ghoul 4, bat 4 | eerie and sorrowful; keeps the dead company |\n807\t\n808\t### 6.6 Knight classes\n809\t\n810\t**Stat rule:**\n811\t- At tier 1, `stat(L) = base + growth × (L − 1)`.\n812\t- At a class change, every stat (MP included) is multiplied by 1.10.\n813\t- After that, growth is ×1.15 (tier 2) or ×1.30 (tier 3) of the line's tier-1 growth.\n814\t- Knights who start at tier 2 or 3 are built the same way with expected values, as if they changed class at levels 10\n815\t  and 20.\n816\t- Bond = base + floor(level / 4). MOV and Ward come from the class.\n817\t\n818\t| id | Class | Line, tier | Weapons | Basic attack | MOV | Ward | Bond | Base at Lv 1: HP/MP/ATK/DEF/INT/AGI | Growth per level | Skills (level) | Next |\n819\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n820\t| squire | Squire | Warrior 1 | sword, spear, axe | Slash 1.0, range 1 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 70/8/17/15/7/11 | 7/.6/1.6/1.4/.4/.9 | Rally (3) | knight at 10 |\n821\t| knight | Knight | Warrior 2 | sword, spear, axe | Slash | 5 | 3 | 7 | ×1.1 at change | ×1.15 | Charge (10), Shield Wall (14) | paladin at 20 + Writ |\n822\t| paladin | Paladin | Warrior 3 | sword, spear | Slash | 5 | 3 | 9 | ×1.1 | ×1.30 | Holy Strike (20), Lay on Hands (24) | — |\n823\t| archer | Archer | Ranger 1 | bow | Shoot 0.9, range 2–4 | 5 | 2 | 4 | 58/10/16/10/9/15 | 5.5/.8/1.5/.9/.6/1.3 | Aimed Shot (4) | ranger at 10 |\n824\t| ranger | Ranger | Ranger 2 | bow | Shoot | 5 | 3 | 6 | | | Volley (10), Pinning Shot (14) | sentinel at 20 + Writ |\n825\t| sentinel | Sentinel | Ranger 3 | bow | Shoot, range 2–5 | 5 | 3 | 7 | | | Piercing Arrow (20), Eagle Eye (24) | — |\n826\t| adept | Adept | Mage 1 | staff, tome | Strike 0.6, range 1 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 50/30/8/8/18/11 | 4.5/2.2/.5/.7/1.8/.9 | own element's Bolt (1), Hex (6) | sorcerer at 10 |\n827\t| sorcerer | Sorcerer | Mage 2 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 6 | | | Storm (10), Mana Siphon (14) | archmage at 20 + Writ |\n828\t| archmage | Archmage | Mage 3 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 7 | | | Tempest (20), Haste (24) | — |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"a728206f-1e46-4501-a7ae-34b5746a7910","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:50:16.794Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/work/PLAN.md","content":"  - `− 1.5 × expected damage to friends`;\n  - `+ 1.2 × healing × (knight ? 2 : 1)`;\n  - `− danger(h) × (knight ? 1.5 : 0.6) × (HP < 40% ? 2 : 1)`, where `danger(h)` is the expected damage foes could deal\n    at `h` next bell;\n  - `− 12` if a monster ends outside its Ward;\n  - `+ 10 × terrain DEF`;\n  - objective terms: from bell 8, attackers `− 2 × distance(h, Keep)` and defending knights `− 3 × distance(h, Keep)`;\n  - when no target is in reach: melee `− 1.2 × distance to the nearest foe`; ranged and casters `− 1.5 × |distance −\n    3|`.\n- Take the best score; ties go to the first in a fixed order.\n- A non-ruler knight below 25% HP whose side is losing on power may Retreat. Rulers never retreat (their danger weight is\n  ×3 instead).\n- Easy picks among its top 3 (weights 3 : 2 : 1); Hard adds +15 for targets already damaged this bell.\n- The same state always gives the same plan, so a bot running both sides is a repeatable test.\n\n### 5.14 Delegate (auto-resolve) and speed\n- **Delegate** runs the same `BattleSim` with the AI on both sides to the end, in one synchronous loop with no drawing,\n  and shows a summary card (losses, captures, level-ups).\n- Animation speed comes from the setting (Full, Fast, Minimal). Holding ✕/Enter during AI turns plays at 4×.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content\n\n### 6.1 The world: Forseason\n- **Shape:** a round continent (radius about 470 world units) on a 1024 × 1024 map (64 × 64 tiles), with the sea all\n  around it.\n- **The centre:** the grey Hour plateau with Meridian, the Calendar City, whose great clock tower is visible from\n  everywhere.\n- **The four quarters, one realm each, each in its native season's look:**\n  - north, Hoarfast: snowfields, pine forests, frozen lakes and the Rimewall mountains;\n  - east, Verdance: green meadows, blossoming orchards, rivers and lakes, spring rain;\n  - south, Solmark: golden savanna, red mesas, dunes and palms along the coast;\n  - west, Amberlyn: amber farmland, oak woods, pumpkin fields, misty bogs and watermills.\n- **The cross-quarter marches** (NE Thaw, SE Beltane, SW Lammas, NW Hallow) blend their two neighbours. Brigand free\n  companies hold them.\n- **The current season tints everything:** a dusting of snow in Winter, blossoms in Spring, gold in Summer, falling\n  leaves in Autumn.\n\n### 6.2 Castles (positions in world units on the 1024 × 1024 map)\n\n| id | Name | Region | Tier | Start owner | Mana | Battle map | Summon circle (tier-1 species; a season in brackets means only then) | Quest site | Treasury | Pos |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| meridian | Meridian, the Calendar City | hour | capital | Dominion | 60 | meridian_clockyard | minute, clockwork, gearhound, stillwraith, pendulumwyrm | The Sleeping Court | Hourglass Rod | 512,512 |\n| midnight | Midnight Keep | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, stillwraith, gearhound | The Bell That Doesn't Ring | Writ of Knighthood | 512,392 |\n| dawnwatch | Dawnwatch | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | hill_fort | minute, clockwork, gearhound | The Sunrise Stair | Swift Spurs | 632,512 |\n| noonspire | Noonspire | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | crossroads | clockwork, gearhound, minute | The Shadowless Square | Signet of Command | 512,632 |\n| vesperhall | Vesper Hall | hour | satellite | Dominion | 30 | ruined_abbey | stillwraith, minute, clockwork | The Evensong Crypt | Writ of Knighthood | 392,512 |\n| rimeholt | Rimeholt | winter | capital | Hoarfast | 40 | capital_citadel | snowkit, frostwolf, icegolem, yeti, frostwyrm (Winter) | The Lake of Silent Bells | Frostplate | 512,92 |\n| wolfsgate | Wolfsgate | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | mountain_pass | frostwolf, snowkit, yeti | The Howling Scar | Winter Shard | 352,235 |\n| frostmere | Frostmere | winter | flank | Hoarfast | 20 | lakeside | snowkit, icegolem, frostwolf | Nimue's Mere | Warding Charm | 672,235 |\n| kestrel | Kestrel Spire | winter | inner | Hoarfast | 25 | forest_hold | frostwolf, yeti, snowkit | The Kestrel Eyrie | Yew Longbow | 512,277 |\n| avalorn | Avalorn | spring | capital | Verdance | 40 | capital_citadel | sproutling, pixie, unicorn, treant, rillserpent (Spring) | The Queen's Orchard | Robe of Seasons | 932,512 |\n| thornwick | Thornwick | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | forest_hold | sproutling, treant, pixie | The Briar Maze | Thornmail | 789,352 |\n| rainmere | Rainmere | spring | flank | Verdance | 20 | river_ford | rillserpent, sproutling, pixie | The Weeping Weir | Spring Seed | 789,672 |\n| primrose | Primrose Ford | spring | inner | Verdance | 25 | lakeside | unicorn, pixie, sproutling | The Unicorn Glade | Tome of Thaw | 747,512 |\n| brazenhold | Brazenhold | summer | capital | Solmark | 40 | capital_citadel | salamander, cinderhound, sunbird, sunmane, wyvern (Summer) | The Furnace Vaults | Sunforged Blade | 512,932 |\n| goldspur | Goldspur | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | crossroads | salamander, cinderhound, wyvern (Summer) | The Wyvern Roost | Summer Ember | 672,789 |\n| cinderwall | Cinderwall | summer | flank | Solmark | 20 | mountain_pass | cinderhound, salamander, sunmane | The Ash Dunes | Mail Hauberk | 352,789 |\n| lionsreach | Lionsreach | summer | inner | Solmark | 25 | hill_fort | sunmane, sunbird, cinderhound | The Lion Steps | Banner Pin | 512,747 |\n| ambergate | Ambergate | autumn | capital | Amberlyn | 40 | capital_citadel | jacklamp, scarecrow, ghoul, tusker, griffin (Autumn) | The Harvest Vault | Lantern Staff | 92,512 |\n| ashbarrow | Ashbarrow | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | ruined_abbey | ghoul, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Barrow Downs | Autumn Acorn | 235,352 |\n| russetmoor | Russetmoor | autumn | flank | Amberlyn | 20 | marsh_keep | tusker, jacklamp, scarecrow | The Russet Bog | Lucky Horseshoe | 235,672 |\n| lanternfall | Lanternfall | autumn | inner | Amberlyn | 25 | forest_hold | jacklamp, ghoul, scarecrow | The Lantern Road | Ring of Mending | 277,512 |\n| thawgate | Thawgate | thaw (winter/spring) | cross | Brigands: Hob Mudspur | 30 | river_ford | snowkit, sproutling, slime, bat | The Breaking Ice | Golden Draught | 756,268 |\n| beltane | Beltane Ford | beltane (spring/summer) | cross | Brigands: Mother Gerrow | 30 | marsh_keep | sproutling, salamander, slime, harpy | The Old Mill of Beltane | Amulet of Tides | 756,756 |\n| lammas | Lammas Cross | lammas (summer/autumn) | cross | Brigands: Red Dafydd | 30 | crossroads | salamander, scarecrow, skeleton, ogre | The Lammas Fair | Thorn Whip | 268,756 |\n| hallowmere | Hallowmere | hallow (autumn/winter) | cross | Brigands: the Hollow Abbot | 30 | ruined_abbey | jacklamp, snowkit, skeleton, bat | The Hollow Abbey Crypts | Hawthorn Bow | 268,268 |\n\nA battle map's dressing (tree kinds, palette, props, castle style) follows the castle's region; terrain then follows the\nbattle's season (§5.11). A cross-quarter castle's season bonus applies in both of its seasons.\n\n### 6.3 Roads (36)\n- **Hoarfast:** rimeholt–wolfsgate, rimeholt–frostmere, wolfsgate–kestrel, frostmere–kestrel.\n- **Verdance:** avalorn–thornwick, avalorn–rainmere, thornwick–primrose, rainmere–primrose.\n- **Solmark:** brazenhold–goldspur, brazenhold–cinderwall, goldspur–lionsreach, cinderwall–lionsreach.\n- **Amberlyn:** ambergate–ashbarrow, ambergate–russetmoor, ashbarrow–lanternfall, russetmoor–lanternfall.\n- **Cross-quarters:** thawgate–frostmere, thawgate–thornwick, beltane–rainmere, beltane–goldspur, lammas–cinderwall,\n  lammas–russetmoor, hallowmere–ashbarrow, hallowmere–wolfsgate.\n- **Into the Hourlands:** kestrel–midnight, primrose–dawnwatch, lionsreach–noonspire, lanternfall–vesperhall.\n- **The Hour ring:** midnight–dawnwatch, dawnwatch–noonspire, noonspire–vesperhall, vesperhall–midnight.\n- **To Meridian:** meridian–midnight, meridian–dawnwatch, meridian–noonspire, meridian–vesperhall.\n\nEvery realm has the same shape: a capital at the back, two flank castles that each face a brigand castle, and an inner\ncastle that faces an Hour satellite. That keeps the realms fair. A test checks the graph is connected and symmetric.\n\n### 6.4 Realms\n\n| id | Realm | Season | Colours (main / trim) | Sigil | Banner | Ruler | Capital |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| verdance | Kingdom of Verdance | Spring | `#4caf50` / `#f0e6c8` | five-petal blossom | swallowtail | Prince Gareth Greenmantle | Avalorn |\n| solmark | Sun-March of Solmark | Summer | `#e0a020` / `#b02a2a` | rayed sun | square | Queen Morgause the Brazen | Brazenhold |\n| amberlyn | Harvest Throne of Amberlyn | Autumn | `#c86a1e` / `#5a3a2a` | oak leaf | pointed | King Pellam the Quiet | Ambergate |\n| hoarfast | Duchy of Hoarfast | Winter | `#6ab0e8` / `#e8f4ff` | snowflake | triangle | Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten | Rimeholt |\n| dominion | Hourless Dominion | Hour | `#3a3a46` / `#d8c070` | hourglass | long tapered | Lord Chancellor Meliant | Meridian |\n| brigands | Free Companies | — | `#7a6a5a` / `#2a2a2a` | crossed axes | ragged | (four captains) | — |\n\nSides are never told apart by colour alone: every unit also carries its realm's sigil on a pennant over it, and the\noutline colour, the banner shape and the sigil all agree.\n\n### 6.5 Knights\nEach row gives the Humanoid look (§7.5) and the voice profile (§9.3). Each troop lists `species level`. Every realm's\ncapital also starts with two tier-1 level-2 monsters in reserve: Verdance sproutlings, Solmark salamanders, Amberlyn\njack-o'-lamps and Hoarfast snowkits. Meridian starts with two level-10 minutes.\n\n#### 6.5.1 Verdance (Spring)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| gareth | **Prince Gareth Greenmantle** (ruler) | Springwarden | 6 | Spring | Avalorn | unicorn 4, pixie 4, sproutling 4 | earnest, idealistic, quick to forgive; grieving his mother, the late Queen | heroic 1.25, armor, short golden hair, circlet, green cape, sword | bright tenor, quick |\n| lynette | Dame Lynette of Thornwick | Squire | 7 | Spring | Thornwick | treant 4, sproutling 3 | his sworn shield; stern, dry humour, protective | heroic 1.2, armor, dark-red ponytail, band, white-and-green tabard | firm alto |\n| pelleas | Sir Pelleas the Lovelorn | Archer | 5 | Spring | Primrose Ford | pixie 4, rillserpent 3 | a poet-archer, overdramatic and brave | heroic 1.15, tunic, long chestnut hair, cap | lilting, high |\n| amris | Brother Amris | Acolyte | 6 | Winter | Avalorn | snowkit 3, sproutling 3 | an old monk from the north; gentle, wry | heroic 1.15, hunch .2, grey robe, bald, staff | slow, low |\n| wren | Wren Ashfeather | Tamer | 5 | Spring | Rainmere | unicorn 3, pixie 3, sproutling 3 | raised among unicorns; few words | heroic 1.1, leaf-green tunic, ash-white spiky hair, hood | chirpy |\n\n#### 6.5.2 Solmark (Summer)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| morgause | **Queen Morgause the Brazen** (ruler) | Sun Sovereign | 7 | Summer | Brazenhold | wyvern 4, cinderhound 4 | magnificent and war-loving, honourable on the field, ruthless at court | heroic 1.3, gold armor, crown, long copper hair, crimson cape, two-handed sword | commanding mezzo |\n| agravain | Sir Agravain Cinderjaw | Squire | 7 | Summer | Cinderwall | cinderhound 4, salamander 3 | a hothead champion who craves glory | bulky 1.25, armor, helmet, red cape | growly baritone |\n| elidure | Captain Elidure of Goldspur | Archer | 6 | Summer | Goldspur | sunbird 3, salamander 3 | disciplined, loyal and secretly kind | heroic 1.2, sand coat, black ponytail, band | clear soprano |\n| hesper | Magus Hesper Vey | Adept | 6 | Hour | Lionsreach | salamander 3, minute 3 | an ambitious court sorcerer who dabbles in Hour magic | heroic 1.2, purple-and-gold robe, pointed hat, long silver hair | silky |\n| brennoc | Old Brennoc | Tamer | 5 | Summer | Brazenhold | sunmane 3, cinderhound 3 | a grizzled, grandfatherly beastkeeper | bulky 1.2, hunch .3, leather coat, bald, whip | gravelly |\n\n#### 6.5.3 Amberlyn (Autumn)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pellam | **King Pellam the Quiet** (ruler) | Harvest King | 8 | Autumn | Ambergate | griffin 4, scarecrow 4 | silent and wise; speaks rarely and briefly; secretly ill | heroic 1.2, hunch .25, amber-and-umber robe, crown, long white hair, staff | soft, low, slow |\n| enid | Lady Enid Russet | Acolyte | 6 | Autumn | Ambergate | jacklamp 3, scarecrow 3 | the king's daughter; gentle, firm, practical | heroic 1.15, cream-and-russet robe, long auburn hair, band | warm |\n| dagonet | Sir Dagonet the Motley | Squire | 5 | Autumn | Russetmoor | tusker 3, jacklamp 3 | a jester-knight who jokes to hide his fear | heroic 1.1, two-colour tunic, pointed hat, sword | bouncy |\n| vesna | Vesna of the Lanterns | Adept | 6 | Summer | Lanternfall | jacklamp 4, ghoul 3 | a lamplighter witch, kind to the dead | heroic 1.15, black-and-orange robe, pointed hat, long black hair | breathy |\n| lamorak | Sir Lamorak Ashbarrow | Squire | 8 | Autumn | Ashbarrow | ghoul 4, scarecrow 3 | a gruff old veteran, loyal to Pellam | bulky 1.2, rusty armor, helmet, brown cape | gruff |\n\n#### 6.5.4 Hoarfast (Winter)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| mordrain | **Duke Mordrain the Frostbitten** (ruler) | Rime Duke | 7 | Winter | Rimeholt | frostwyrm 3, snowkit 4 | theatrical, mad and brilliant; speaks in riddles; grief hidden under ice | heroic 1.25, white coat, icicle crown, long white hair, staff, pale-blue cape, faint eyeGlow | high, erratic pitch |\n| ragnell | Dame Ragnell Ice-Eye | Squire | 8 | Winter | Kestrel Spire | frostwolf 4, icegolem 3 | his cold, calculating marshal, the sane one | heroic 1.25, steel armor, helmet, white ponytail, dark-blue cape | flat alto |\n| safir | Sir Safir the Pale | Archer | 6 | Winter | Wolfsgate | frostwolf 3, snowkit 3 | a quiet, melancholic hunter | heroic 1.2, white hood, grey coat | soft |\n| nimue | Nimue of Frostmere | Adept | 7 | Winter | Frostmere | snowkit 4, snowkit 3 | an enigmatic lake witch who makes bargains | heroic 1.15, teal robe, long pale-blue hair | echoing |\n| gorm | Gorm the Bear | Tamer | 5 | Autumn | Rimeholt | yeti 3, tusker 3 | huge and gentle; raised in the western woods | bulky 1.35, brown fur coat, short hair, whip | very low |\n\n#### 6.5.5 The Hourless Dominion (Hour)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Castle | Troop | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| meliant | **Lord Chancellor Meliant** (ruler) | Chancellor of Hours | 14 | Meridian | pendulumwyrm 10, clockwork (tier 2: Tick Knight) 12, stillwraith 12 | cold, grieving and absolute; believes he is merciful | heroic 1.25, black-and-brass robe, brass band, short grey hair, brass rod | measured baritone |\n| bertilak | Marshal Bertilak the Hourward | Knight | 12 | Midnight Keep | clockwork (tier 2) 12, gearhound 10, gearhound 9 | courteous, ruthless; loves a duel | bulky 1.3, brass armor, helmet, green-black cape | booming |\n| aurelie | Countess Aurelie of Vespers | Sorcerer | 12 | Vesper Hall | stillwraith 10, minute 10, minute 9 | elegant, bored and cruel | heroic 1.2, violet-and-black robe, long black hair, band | drawling |\n| morholt | Sir Morholt the Unmoving | Knight | 11 | Noonspire | clockwork 10, clockwork 9 | a silent giant | bulky 1.45, black armor, helmet | grunts only |\n| tic | Tic | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | a clockwork twin who finishes Tac's sentences | chibi 1.0, brass armor, cap | squeaky, high |\n| tac | Tac | Ranger | 10 | Dawnwatch | gearhound 9, minute 9 | the other twin | the same, colours swapped | squeaky, low |\n| graynight | **The Gray Knight, Sir Nonesuch** | Knight of the Thirteenth Hour | 25 | the Sanctum only | minute (tier 3) 22 ×4, pendulumwyrm (tier 2) 22 | the month that never was: calm, ancient, faintly amused | heroic 1.6, grey armor, helmet, tattered grey cape, white eyeGlow, long sword, clock-hand halo | two detuned low voices |\n\nThe Gray Knight's stats are fixed: HP 900, MP 200, ATK 52, DEF 48, INT 50, AGI 30, MOV 5. His skills are Thirteenth\nStroke, Still, Unmaking and Timeless.\n\n#### 6.5.6 Free knights (joined by event or quest)\n\n| id | Name | Class | Lv | Elem | How they join | Brings | Who they are | Look | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| lunete | Princess Lunete of Meridian | Hourmaiden | 8 | Hour | the Lunete chain (§6.12) | — | the Keeper's daughter; steady and kind; carries her father's broken watch | heroic 1.15, white-and-brass robe, long gold hair, band | clear, gentle |\n| galeron | Sir Galeron the Wanderer | Knight | 10 | Spring | Wanderer outcome at Winter or Spring sites, from Autumn of Year 1 | frostwolf 8 | an errant knight looking for a cause | heroic 1.25, dented armor, faded green cape | weary tenor |\n| blanchefleur | Blanchefleur the Sellsword | Ranger | 10 | Autumn | Wanderer at Summer or Autumn sites, or the Lammas Fair (pay 150 mana) | sunmane 8 | a mercenary with a code: coin first | heroic 1.2, red-brown coat, short blonde hair | brisk |\n| owain | Owain the Dragonless | Beastlord | 11 | Summer | event `owain`: the first time your realm binds a wyvern or frost wyrm | — | lost his dragon in the Long Winter; will train yours | bulky 1.25, leather coat, short hair | husky |\n| ettard | Sister Ettard | Priest | 10 | Winter | Wanderer at Hallowmere, Lanternfall or Frostmere | snowkit 7 | a sharp-tongued healer | heroic 1.15, white-and-blue robe, hood | crisp |\n\n#### 6.5.7 Brigand captains (Brigand Captain class)\n\n| id | Name | Lv | Elem | Castle | Troop | Who they are |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| hob | Hob Mudspur | 5 | Winter | Thawgate | snowkit 4, frostwolf 4, bat 3, slime 3 | swaggering, and a coward at heart |\n| gerrow | Mother Gerrow | 5 | Spring | Beltane Ford | slime 4, harpy 4, sproutling 3, bat 3 | motherly and crafty; hides Lunete at her mill |\n| dafydd | Red Dafydd | 6 | Summer | Lammas Cross | ogre 4, skeleton 4, salamander 3 | boisterous and proud |\n| abbot | The Hollow Abbot | 6 | Autumn | Hallowmere | skeleton 5, ghoul 4, bat 4 | eerie and sorrowful; keeps the dead company |\n\n### 6.6 Knight classes\n\n**Stat rule:**\n- At tier 1, `stat(L) = base + growth × (L − 1)`.\n- At a class change, every stat (MP included) is multiplied by 1.10.\n- After that, growth is ×1.15 (tier 2) or ×1.30 (tier 3) of the line's tier-1 growth.\n- Knights who start at tier 2 or 3 are built the same way with expected values, as if they changed class at levels 10\n  and 20.\n- Bond = base + floor(level / 4). MOV and Ward come from the class.\n\n| id | Class | Line, tier | Weapons | Basic attack | MOV | Ward | Bond | Base at Lv 1: HP/MP/ATK/DEF/INT/AGI | Growth per level | Skills (level) | Next |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| squire | Squire | Warrior 1 | sword, spear, axe | Slash 1.0, range 1 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 70/8/17/15/7/11 | 7/.6/1.6/1.4/.4/.9 | Rally (3) | knight at 10 |\n| knight | Knight | Warrior 2 | sword, spear, axe | Slash | 5 | 3 | 7 | ×1.1 at change | ×1.15 | Charge (10), Shield Wall (14) | paladin at 20 + Writ |\n| paladin | Paladin | Warrior 3 | sword, spear | Slash | 5 | 3 | 9 | ×1.1 | ×1.30 | Holy Strike (20), Lay on Hands (24) | — |\n| archer | Archer | Ranger 1 | bow | Shoot 0.9, range 2–4 | 5 | 2 | 4 | 58/10/16/10/9/15 | 5.5/.8/1.5/.9/.6/1.3 | Aimed Shot (4) | ranger at 10 |\n| ranger | Ranger | Ranger 2 | bow | Shoot | 5 | 3 | 6 | | | Volley (10), Pinning Shot (14) | sentinel at 20 + Writ |\n| sentinel | Sentinel | Ranger 3 | bow | Shoot, range 2–5 | 5 | 3 | 7 | | | Piercing Arrow (20), Eagle Eye (24) | — |\n| adept | Adept | Mage 1 | staff, tome | Strike 0.6, range 1 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 50/30/8/8/18/11 | 4.5/2.2/.5/.7/1.8/.9 | own element's Bolt (1), Hex (6) | sorcerer at 10 |\n| sorcerer | Sorcerer | Mage 2 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 6 | | | Storm (10), Mana Siphon (14) | archmage at 20 + Writ |\n| archmage | Archmage | Mage 3 | staff, tome | Strike | 4 | 3 | 7 | | | Tempest (20), Haste (24) | — |","numLines":200,"startLine":629,"totalLines":2404}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Cqeo7YbcKyUGTxz75CUXDy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
