{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C1tUVeJcjQNgnkSio5MwJJ","type":"tool_result","content":"14:## 0. At a glance\n65:## 1. From the source to this game\n67:### 1.1 What makes Brigandine distinctive, and what it becomes here\n88:### 1.2 Originality guardrails\n98:## 2. Folders, build and the working environment\n142:## 3. Architecture\n144:### 3.1 Layers\n167:### 3.2 Source files (concatenated in this order)\n212:### 3.3 What the engine provides (use it; don't rebuild it)\n227:### 3.4 Planned engine changes (log each one in ENGINE-CHANGES.md)\n240:### 3.5 Saves, settings and tunables\n250:### 3.6 Scenes and deep links\n257:### 3.7 `game.debug` (the handle tests and tools read)\n266:## 4. Campaign rules (`CampaignSim`)\n268:### 4.1 Calendar and the Hour-Candle\n276:### 4.2 Seasons outside battle\n284:### 4.3 The three phases of a season\n300:### 4.4 Castles\n306:### 4.5 Mana\n313:### 4.6 Summon\n319:### 4.7 Bind (Organize)\n325:### 4.8 Move\n329:### 4.9 Quests\n347:### 4.10 Equip and items\n354:### 4.11 Promotions and class changes (Muster only, with an animation and a jingle)\n361:### 4.12 Declaring a march\n369:### 4.13 Resolution\n380:### 4.14 Aftermath\n395:### 4.15 Campaign AI (`23-ai-campaign.js`, deterministic per seed)\n429:### 4.16 Stillness\n434:### 4.17 Winning and losing\n446:### 4.18 Difficulty (chosen for each new campaign)\n458:## 5. Battle rules (`BattleSim`)\n460:### 5.1 The field\n467:### 5.2 Sides and deployment\n477:### 5.3 Bells and turn order\n489:### 5.4 A unit's turn\n506:### 5.5 Stats\n514:### 5.6 Formulas (every constant is in `G.tune`, Appendix A)\n545:### 5.7 Terrain\n570:### 5.8 Effects (statuses, buffs and debuffs)\n588:### 5.9 Knights falling, retreat, capture and death\n601:### 5.10 Winning\n607:### 5.11 Seasons in battle (the Forseasons rules)\n617:### 5.12 Forecast\n622:### 5.13 Battle AI (`21-ai-battle.js`)\n644:### 5.14 Delegate (auto-resolve) and speed\n651:## 6. Content\n653:### 6.1 The world: Forseason\n668:### 6.2 Castles (positions in world units on the 1024 × 1024 map)\n701:### 6.3 Roads (36)\n715:### 6.4 Realms\n729:### 6.5 Knights\n734:#### 6.5.1 Verdance (Spring)\n744:#### 6.5.2 Solmark (Summer)\n754:#### 6.5.3 Amberlyn (Autumn)\n764:#### 6.5.4 Hoarfast (Winter)\n774:#### 6.5.5 The Hourless Dominion (Hour)\n789:#### 6.5.6 Free knights (joined by event or quest)\n799:#### 6.5.7 Brigand captains (Brigand Captain class)\n808:### 6.6 Knight classes\n847:### 6.7 Skills and spells\n937:### 6.8 Bestiary (30 species, 3 forms each)\n979:### 6.9 Items (33; there are no shops: items come from quests, events and castle treasuries)\n1020:### 6.10 Battle maps (13)\n1226:### 6.11 Quest sites (one per castle; a quest is sent from the castle itself, and a story site from any owned castl\n1275:### 6.12 Story\n1277:#### 6.12.1 Premise (the back-story the scripts assume)\n1295:#### 6.12.2 Style guide (match the source's register)\n1309:#### 6.12.3 How events run\n1323:#### 6.12.4 Scripts (write these as given; the rest follow the beats in §6.12.5)\n1423:#### 6.12.5 Event list (beats; write each scene in the style above)\n1471:#### 6.12.6 Rival lines (2 lines before a battle when both are on the field; the first match plays)\n1486:### 6.13 Tutorial: \"The Border Road\" (Border Meadow, Spring)\n1505:## 7. Presentation: art, rendering and animation\n1507:### 7.1 Look target and palettes\n1524:### 7.2 The battlefield (`31-art-hexfield.js`)\n1587:### 7.3 The world map (`32-art-worldmap.js`)\n1630:### 7.4 Story stages (`64-scene-event.js`)\n1649:### 7.5 Units (`33-art-units.js`, `engine-ext/beasts.js`)\n1733:### 7.6 Effects (`34-art-fx.js`)\n1757:### 7.7 Animation checklist (each gets a filmstrip or gallery look, §14)\n1768:## 8. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n1770:### 8.1 Rules for every screen\n1783:### 8.2 The input map (the game's own preset per scene; the engine keeps its menu keys)\n1806:### 8.3 Prompts and glyphs\n1820:### 8.4 The focus model (`50-ui-kit.js`