{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3s7bzMZDzFnXC4ZSvr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CixvZx29XV5b9qZSwT8XKG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == count, (old[:60], s.count(old))\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# designer-facing data\nrep(\"\"\"  realm, song, voice`. A validation suite checks that every id a spec refers to exists. Content never edits the code\n  that runs it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  realm, song, voice`. A validation suite checks that every id a spec refers to exists. Content never edits the code\n  that runs it. This is how the rest of the game gets built later with ordinary designer tools: tables, ASCII maps and\n  story nodes that a designer edits and the `data` suite checks, plus dev mode's jump, trigger and gallery tools to try\n  any piece in seconds.\"\"\")\n\n# performance budget\nrep(\"\"\"Battle ambient light by season: Spring .8 (cool green), Summer .95 (warm), Autumn .7 (amber), Winter .65 (blue). The\nHour places are dark (.45): brass lamps and the clock's glow light them.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Battle ambient light by season: Spring .8 (cool green), Summer .95 (warm), Autumn .7 (amber), Winter .65 (blue). The\nHour places are dark (.45): brass lamps and the clock's glow light them.\n\nTASK.md treats the performance budget as unlimited, and FPS targets and optimization are out of scope. Add the detail,\nlights, shadows, weather and effects each scene needs, and spend no time on frame-rate work.\"\"\")\n\n# attract scope\nrep(\"\"\"- **The title** (§8.5.1) tracks idle time: any key, mouse button, pointer move over 4 px, pad button, stick past .5 or\n  touch resets it. At 10 s it goes to `attract`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **The title** (§8.5.1) and the setup menus before play (campaign setup, skirmish setup) track idle time: any key,\n  mouse button, pointer move over 4 px, pad button, stick past .5 or touch resets it. At 10 s they go to `attract`.\n  Reading screens (About, How to Play) and anything in play never do.\"\"\")\n\n# no subagents for review\nrep(\"\"\"- The Node harness loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine-ext/beasts.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the\n  stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). It drives the game with `game.advance`,\n  `input.tap` / `hold` / `feed` and `game.debug`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- The Node harness loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine-ext/beasts.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the\n  stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). It drives the game with `game.advance`,\n  `input.tap` / `hold` / `feed` and `game.debug`.\n- As TASK.md asks: test with headless tools and scripts that play the game and read its state; take screenshots only\n  for what a script can't check (§14.4); rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (§14.7); and don't use\n  subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF","description":"Insert four clarifications required by TASK.md into PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":614064,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":725},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67","uuid":"55b67d05-381e-4b9a-8468-7baab5150545","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:51:43.494Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3s7JPaT11AqcZVkBNc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CixvZx29XV5b9qZSwT8XKG":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-mat